{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:37:30.178Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019fd4ee-d6c2-7b01-895c-7daab9d10d8a","call_id":"call_HTFCEOe802PAO6toCSlQJhar","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/complete_manifest\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/docker_preflight_diagnosis\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Core source behavior is clean for authorization, tenant isolation, direct-link outcomes, template structure, and announcement targeting.\\n\\nOne confirmed defect remains:\\n\\n- `events:viewPublic` is still presented as a configurable permission in `src/shared/permissions/permissions.ts`, but no runtime path enforces it. Remove this misleading no-op permission and its seed/test references.\\n\\nStack caveat:\\n\\n- The discovery commit removes `unlisted` and old listing permissions while Playwright/generated-documentation sources still reference them. The planned replacement patch must directly follow or be folded into that slice; otherwise intermediate PRs are not independently full-suite compliant.\\n\\nAll patches satisfy review limits: 3/23/34/33 files and 100/113/740/1,242 changed lines.\\n\\nRemaining proof gaps are PostgreSQL-backed discovery/role-transition checks and Browser/Playwright verification of direct-link and announcement journeys.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/final_verification_matrix\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/stack_ui_test_layers\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/stack_ui_test_layers/align_admin_copy_tests\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/stack_ui_test_layers/audit_generated_guard/fix_platform_authority_guard\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_me