{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:32:51.777Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The permanent Docker fix is now proven against the real failure mode: a hard project-only rebuild completes, and `docker:resume` restarts the same containers while preserving the successful setup jobs. I’m moving back to the review-stack gate audit; one genuine intermediate test inconsistency was found in the safe-error layer, and I’ll fold its test expectation into that owning layer rather than add another PR.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:32:51.777Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a740e720c608191a43965fd85c78f29","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The permanent Docker fix is now proven against the real failure mode: a hard project-only rebuild completes, and `docker:resume` restarts the same containers while preserving the successful setup jobs. I’m moving back to the review-stack gate audit; one genuine intermediate test inconsistency was found in the safe-error layer, and I’ll fold its test expectation into that owning layer rather than add another PR."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:32:52.633Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a740e73c7a08191a5f688711fbe8d30","status":"completed","call_id":"call_AjgkzUsuA5I0WVZHWWLTbE7Q","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"gh stack --help && gh stack status --json | jq '{currentBranch, stacks: [.stacks[]? | {branches: [.branches[]? | {name, sha, parent}]}]}'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:32:52.885Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd558-7895-74c0-90a3-1aa040ace0c7","call_id":"call_AjgkzUsuA5I0WVZHWWLTbE7Q","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Stacked PRs let you break a large change into a chain of pull requests\nthat build on each other. Use `gh stack` to create and manage your stack\nlocally, then push to GitHub to create your stack of PRs.\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack [command]\n\nExamples:\n  # Start a new stack targeting your default branch\n  $ gh stack init\n\n  # Or turn an existing set of branches into a stack\n  $ gh stack init branch1 branch2 branch3\n\n  # Make changes and commit, then add a branch to the stack\n  $ gh stack add branch4\n\n  # Push all branches and create/update PRs on GitHub\n  $ gh stack submit\n\n  # Keep your local in sync with remote\n  $ gh stack sync\n\nStack management:\n  add         Add a new branch on top of the current stack\n  checkout    Checkout a stack by stack number, PR number, PR URL, or branch name\n  init        Initialize a new stack\n  modify      Interactively restructure a stack\n  unstack     Remove a stack locally and on GitHub\n  view        View the current stack\n\nRemote operations:\n  link        Link PRs into a stack on GitHub without local tracking\n  merge       Merge a stack of pull requests\n  push        Push active branches in the current stack to the remote\n  rebase      Rebase a stack of branches\n  submit      Create a stack of PRs on GitHub\n  sync        Sync the current stack with the remote\n\nNavigation:\n  bottom      Check out the bottom branch of the stack (closest to the trunk)\n  down        Check out a branch further down in the stack (closer to the trunk)\n  switch      Interactively switch to another branch in the stack\n  top         Check out the top branch of the stack (furthest from the trunk)\n  trunk       Check out the trunk branch of the stack\n  up          Check out a branch further up in the stack (further from the trunk)\n\nUtilities:\n  alias       Create a shell alias for gh stack\n  feedback    Submit feedback for gh-stack\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help      help for stack\n  -v, --version   version for stack\n\nUse \"gh stack [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nLearn more:\n  Documentation: https://gh.io/stacks\n  Feedback: https://gh.io/stacks-feedback\nunknown flag: --json\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
