{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:33:20.916Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a740e9014cc8191b27fc3c939cb43f2","status":"completed","call_id":"call_zpNVGrAgUsLRj3c8wVm68x7H","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"gh stack modify --help && gh stack add --help && gh stack init --help && sed -n '1,260p' \\\"$(git rev-parse --git-dir)/gh-stack\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:33:21.149Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd558-e6fd-7e73-a558-3557704dec72","call_id":"call_zpNVGrAgUsLRj3c8wVm68x7H","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Open an interactive TUI to restructure the current stack.\n\nOperations available:\n  • Drop branches from the stack\n  • Fold branches into adjacent branches\n  • Insert new branches into the stack\n  • Reorder branches\n  • Rename branches\n\nAll changes are staged in the TUI and applied together when you press Ctrl+S.\nIf your changes affect branches with pull requests, run 'gh stack submit'\nafterward to push changes, update PRs, and recreate the stack on GitHub.\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack modify [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  # Open the interactive TUI to restructure the stack\n  $ gh stack modify\n\n  # Abort a modify session and restore the stack\n  $ gh stack modify --abort\n\n  # Continue after resolving conflicts from a modify\n  $ gh stack modify --continue\n\nFlags:\n      --abort      Abort the modify session and restore the stack to its pre-modify state\n      --continue   Continue after resolving conflicts\n  -h, --help       help for modify\nAdd a new branch on top of the current stack.\n\nWhen -m is omitted but -A or -u is used, your editor opens for the\ncommit message. When -m is provided without an explicit branch name,\nthe branch name is auto-generated from the commit message.\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack add [branch] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  # Add a new named branch to the stack\n  $ gh stack add my-feature\n\n  # Add a branch and commit staged changes\n  $ gh stack add -Am \"Add user authentication\" my-feature\n\n  # Auto-generate branch name from the commit message\n  $ gh stack add -m \"Fix login bug\"\n  \n  # Add a branch and open editor to write commit message\n  $ gh stack add -A my-feature\n\nFlags:\n  -A, --all              Stage all changes including untracked files\n  -h, --help             help for add\n  -m, --message string   Create a commit with this message\n  -u, --update           Stage changes to tracked files only\nInitialize a new stack of branches in the current repository.\n\nYou can pass multiple branch names to create a multi-layer stack in one\ncommand. Existing branches are adopted automatically; missing branches are\ncreated. By default, the first branch is based on the default branch, and\neach subsequent branch is based on the previous one.\n\nUse --base to specify a different trunk branch.\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack init [branches...] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  # Create a stack with a new branch\n  $ gh stack init my-feature\n\n  # Create a multi-layer stack at once\n  $ gh stack init auth-layer api-routes ui-components\n\n  # Adopt existing branches into a stack (bottom to top)\n  $ gh stack init feat/auth feat/api feat/ui\n\n  # Specify a different trunk branch\n  $ gh stack init --base develop my-feature\n\nFlags:\n  -b, --base string   Trunk branch for stack (defaults to default branch)\n  -h, --help          help for init\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"repository\": \"github.com:evorto-app/app\",\n  \"stacks\": [\n    {\n      \"trunk\": {\n        \"branch\": \"main\",\n        \"head\": \"d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea\"\n      },\n      \"branches\": [\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-prior-compliance-artifacts\",\n          \"head\": \"3c1ea2e0a0cd33a20b8e1495eef7c4f6f25c14fa\",\n          \"base\": \"d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-dead-runtime-dependencies\",\n          \"head\": \"efd348a4cb506efb9ab1dd91d25e758e30bbd57b\",\n          \"base\": \"3c1ea2e0a0cd33a20b8e1495eef7c4f6f25c14fa\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-legacy-migration-tools\",\n          \"head\": \"8eab254e9d849344b7662650f053522cfbf000d4\",\n          \"base\": \"efd348a4cb506efb9ab1dd91d25e758e30bbd57b\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-tenant-migration-steps\",\n          \"head\": \"7c6e4b52a6a98f1664382a2aebb7fb024400b679\",\n          \"base\": \"8eab254e9d849344b7662650f053522cfbf000d4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-identity-migration-steps\",\n          \"head\": \"b019239b48041e7258a8154ffbb2321f6898c04d\",\n          \"base\": \"7c6e4b52a6a98f1664382a2aebb7fb024400b679\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-event-migration-steps\",\n          \"head\": \"070bc64979373d37824876652cb2a0482b969cb8\",\n          \"base\": \"b019239b48041e7258a8154ffbb2321f6898c04d\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-legacy-event-mapping-rules\",\n          \"head\": \"7ec7b7f832a21faa544459932a3da3400280a238\",\n          \"base\": \"070bc64979373d37824876652cb2a0482b969cb8\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-migration-support-utilities\",\n          \"head\": \"aa68eafd30be93834c3c1c688405f6e736e036fc\",\n          \"base\": \"7ec7b7f832a21faa544459932a3da3400280a238\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-migration-repository-wiring\",\n          \"head\": \"fada8ab8cf428e7eda8715aec7f71efb4a41a3c9\",\n          \"base\": \"aa68eafd30be93834c3c1c688405f6e736e036fc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-legacy-schema-module\",\n          \"head\": \"96e747d3cb61571213bef0b808d04bb664ced818\",\n          \"base\": \"fada8ab8cf428e7eda8715aec7f71efb4a41a3c9\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-legacy-schema-history\",\n          \"head\": \"9b0a3a41ee8cf74089383e561a44b9b82b83938c\",\n          \"base\": \"96e747d3cb61571213bef0b808d04bb664ced818\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-generated-legacy-snapshot\",\n          \"head\": \"9563aa977d483fa95e43405aa5b112bdc840f8cc\",\n          \"base\": \"9b0a3a41ee8cf74089383e561a44b9b82b83938c\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/remove-invalid-types-alias\",\n          \"head\": \"bdf061bcc72dc0b08f17fa39ed490fb3de1b3c57\",\n          \"base\": \"9563aa977d483fa95e43405aa5b112bdc840f8cc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/guard-local-drizzle-targets\",\n          \"head\": \"7796ffb2acebf641be3ab40f76053d4db7d796d6\",\n          \"base\": \"bdf061bcc72dc0b08f17fa39ed490fb3de1b3c57\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/require-explicit-seed-context\",\n          \"head\": \"d683bad1215f5a79b7c45415901c2c5f66df08a9\",\n          \"base\": \"7796ffb2acebf641be3ab40f76053d4db7d796d6\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/fail-closed-local-seeding\",\n          \"head\": \"de9d4bb422659162e94580268b3213ba1ebc2c8a\",\n          \"base\": \"d683bad1215f5a79b7c45415901c2c5f66df08a9\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/reuse-primary-provider-credentials\",\n          \"head\": \"6ee7155a1e28f66e5c1cf2c77a276c0b416e889e\",\n          \"base\": \"de9d4bb422659162e94580268b3213ba1ebc2c8a\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/harden-brand-asset-storage\",\n          \"head\": \"61b95981b79faff377e93c48ef5d74824227eeff\",\n          \"base\": \"6ee7155a1e28f66e5c1cf2c77a276c0b416e889e\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/use-production-shaped-tenant-fixtures\",\n          \"head\": \"84afc253657d8f6736f4b33b04c139f310c63885\",\n          \"base\": \"61b95981b79faff377e93c48ef5d74824227eeff\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/fail-closed-local-runtime-state\",\n          \"head\": \"338cef45e170a2c0aeafa48e284d5263f49d2fd2\",\n          \"base\": \"84afc253657d8f6736f4b33b04c139f310c63885\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"branch\": \"codex/harden-container-runtime-image\",\n          \"head\": \"f1e52da4f0ab9adfbb3582c58680da21d621e030\",\n          \"base\": \"338cef45e170a2c0aeafa48e284d5263f49d