historical phrase\n  list to visible Angular template/copy-helper text, every rendered email\n  variant, public domain and safe internal-error messages, and bundled guide\n  prose. The expanded guard surfaced and removed remaining event-creation,\n  organization-image, and transfer diagnostics instead of hiding them behind\n  generic fallback copy.\n- 2026-08-05: The final complete guide run's fail-loud capture guard exposed\n  one profile screenshot taken before account details were ready. The journey\n  now proves that exact completed state before capture; its focused 8/8 run and\n  the full 51/51 guide run pass without a retry, delay, or screenshot fallback.\n- 2026-08-05: The final read-only gate found a superseded interactive overview,\n  storage-oriented guide phrases, and enforcement gaps for inline/shared\n  application copy plus Setext or raw HTML guide titles. The old overview was\n  removed, the current 151-finding/41-candidate overview replaced it, and the\n  wording and structure guards were extended without a retry, compatibility\n  path, or generic recovery layer.\n- 2026-08-05: Reopened the final documentation proof after recognizing that the\n  last successful 51/51 run preceded the final copy and guard edits. A clean\n  rerun could not start because Docker's database-container start remained\n  blocked while setting up the read-only `ops/local-postgres-init.sql` mount.\n  The unrelated project was left unchanged, a second stack or partial proof was\n  rejected as a fallback, and RQ-015 remains in progress until Docker Desktop\n  can be restarted deliberately.\n- 2026-08-05: Traced that Docker start block to Docker Desktop waiting in host\n  path inspection for the worktree's read-only PostgreSQL initialization-file\n  mount. Removed the mount and moved integration-database creation into the\n  explicit setup step, where failures remain visible. Two clean empty-volume\n  starts, 48/48 then 7/7 focused tests, the 17-file/83-test PostgreSQL suite,\n  and a state-preserving stop/resume cycle passed. The unrelated Docker project\n  retained its exact intended state.\n- 2026-08-05: Rebuilt the current application and completed the final 51/51\n  documentation run. Its 35 pages reference 183 unique screenshots with zero\n  missing or orphaned files; all 183 images decode, none are blank or low\n  contrast, and OCR found no technical, loading, test, browser, or internal\n  wording. The only four web addresses are intentional public organization\n  branding, membership-card, and privacy examples.\n- 2026-08-05: The exact-current-tree functional run surfaced one stale\n  documentation-reporter assertion after 152 other journeys passed. Removed\n  the superseded technical wording from that test contract rather than adding\n  an alias; the complete rerun then passed 153/153 with no failures, skips,\n  retries, or incomplete tests.\n- 2026-08-05: Settled D-008 by explicitly allowing one payment account to serve\n  multiple organizations. Each attachment and every payment action remains\n  organization-scoped; no cross-organization uniqueness, lookup, access, or\n  compatibility path was added.\n- 2026-08-05: Recovered the two ESNcard examples and Google Maps value already\n  present in the primary checkout. The test commands now fill only those exact\n  missing names in memory, never print or copy their values, and never import\n  database, authentication, port, or other checkout settings. Missing values\n  still stop the normal preflight visibly.\n- 2026-08-05: The complete publication run surfaced a stale Google Maps guide\n  name and one premature role-page capture. Corrected the catalog directly and\n  waited for the role page to finish becoming interactive; no alias, retry,\n  timeout increase, or fallback was added. The official rerun passed 54/54,\n  published all 13 guides and 199 assets, and removed all five retired guide\n  destinations.\n- 2026-08-05: The final live ESNcard run exposed a stale anchored status\n  matcher and stale empty-state copy in the functional journey; the application\n  had rendered the verified card correctly. Removed the unnecessary cache\n  experiment, then made the journey wait for hydration, poll the persisted\n  status, and prove that `lastCheckedAt` advances. The release command passed 8\n  focused unit checks and all 9 provider-backed Playwright journeys without a\n  retry, delay, or product fallback.\n- 2026-08-05: The complete functional baseline surfaced F-155: the tax-rate\n  import action appeared enabled in server-rendered output before the page was\n  ready to handle its click. The journey now waits for the existing readiness\n  marker to clear and clicks once. No second click, delay, weakened assertion,\n  or product fallback was added; the full rerun passed 153/153.\n- 2026-08-05: Confirmed the local Docker lifecycle boundary. The persistent\n  worktree stack and Playwright's disposable stack cannot own the same project\n  at once. The reliable sequence is to stop the persistent stack before\n  Playwright and recreate it before PostgreSQL verification. The first final\n  PostgreSQL command received `ECONNREFUSED` after Playwright intentionally\n  removed its stack; an explicit `docker:start` followed by the unchanged\n  command passed all 17 files and 83 tests. This is an operating-order fix, not\n  an application-code fix, and the unrelated `evorto-cda27261` project remained\n  untouched.\n- 2026-08-05: The first final image build overlapped other heavy application and\n  Docker builds, exhausted Docker's available memory, and ended with exit 137.\n  It produced no usable image-security result. No code fix or fallback is\n  claimed. After the heavy gates were serialized, the isolated unchanged rerun\n  built the 95,726,857-byte linux/amd64 image, excluded runtime source maps,\n  exported them separately, and found zero vulnerabilities.\n- 2026-08-05: Closed the exact-current-tree gate: the frozen local install made\n  no changes; format, lint, 144-file/1,106-test Angular, 199-file/1,603-test\n  server, build, release validation, 11/11 integration journeys, and Terraform\n  bootstrap, production, and staging with zero misconfigurations pass. The\n  provider-backed publication passed 54/54 and produced 13 guides with 199\n  assets. The live ESNcard release check passed 8 focused unit checks and all 9\n  journeys.\n- 2026-08-05: Final visual inspection surfaced F-156 in the first-steps guide:\n  an email caption accompanied a full-page image that also exposed the password\n  form and internal test-environment branding. The source journey now requests\n  an optional exact-element crop, asserts that `person@example.org` is visible\n  and editable before one capture, then restores the real one-time account. No\n  generated-page patch, retry, fallback, or application behavior change was\n  added. The corrected official publication passed 54/54 and copied 13 guides\n  with 199 assets. The exact neutral crop was visually inspected; Pages tooling\n  passed 19/19 with lint, `git diff --check`, and the 23-page build.\n\n### Reconstructed 99-layer stack checkpoint\n\n- 2026-08-05: Replayed 80 focused application-source layers from\n  `d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea`. Each has one intended branch,\n  a lowercase conventional type, and fewer than 100 files and at most 1,500\n  changed lines, except the approved one-file `+0/-3062` generated legacy\n  snapshot deletion. Changed release notes contain none of the forbidden\n  implementation terms.\n- 2026-08-05: Added the focused platform-administration contract layer at\n  position 81. It changes 8 files by +420/-26, rejects incomplete or oversized\n  audit data visibly, and keeps target authority explicit.\n- 2026-08-05: Replayed the exact 12-layer UI, guide, and acceptance series at\n  positions 82-93. Every rewritten commit reproduces its expected tree; the\n  largest layer is 1,400 changed lines and the widest is 83 files. The final\n  series passes 134 Angular files/966 tests, 187 server files/1,497 tests,\n  `build:app`, formatting, lint, diff and wording guards, with zero active\n  skip/fixme controls outside the detector's own fixture strings.\n- 2026-08-05: Added F-157 by deleting the unused configurable\n  `events:viewPublic` capability and every old ordinary listing-state reference.\n  Ordinary event discovery still follows D-003, and role-targeted announcements\n  still follow D-004; no compatibility alias or fallback path was added.\n- 2026-08-05: Added F-158 at position 94. Ordinary start, stop, status, resume,\n  watch, foreground, and Playwright teardown operations now have one bounded,\n  fail-visible path. Teardown verifies once and returns the first failure instead\n  of retrying. The final layer changes 8 files by +479/-141; `bash -n`,\n  `git diff --check`, and 45/45 focused Vitest tests pass without touching a\n  real Docker project.\n- 2026-08-05: Prepared this queue as the sole position-95 file and independently\n  replayed the four positions 96-99 after the exact UI and Docker trees. Their\n  structural sizes remain 7 files/300 lines, 2/764, 3/113, and 5/608. They do\n  not touch this queue. Their final shared commit and tree IDs are deliberately\n  absent until position 95 exists.\n- 2026-08-05: Started canonical exact-head validation for the reconstructed\n  branches. Early parallel server runs produced fixed five-second worker-start\n  timeouts under excess local concurrency; those runs are provisional failures,\n  not passes and not product defects. They must be rerun sequentially. No timeout\n  increase, retry wrapper, reduced test selection, or CI substitution is\n  accepted as final evidence.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\n### Reconstructed-stack evidence\n\n- Exact structural checkpoint: 94 committed layers through\n  `571e511252bc2d03ddcf385ac34d2ebbfdd308d9`, with exactly one intended branch\n  per layer, no empty/fixup/temp layer, and all file/line limits satisfied.\n- Position 81: 8 files, +420/-26, one intended branch, clean diff and plain\n  release note.\n- Positions 82-93: exact-tree 12-patch replay; 134 Angular files/966 tests and\n  187 server files/1,497 tests pass with zero incomplete tests; build, format,\n  lint, aggregate diff, visible-wording, generated-guide, and active-skip\n  guards pass.\n- Position 94: 8 files, +479/-141; shell syntax, diff check, and the configured\n  Vitest run for all three changed test files pass 45/45. No real Docker state\n  was changed for this focused proof.\n- Prepared positions 96-99 apply cleanly after the exact final UI and Docker\n  tree and remain within all structural limits. Their source-series validation\n  passed formatting, lint, action syntax, shell syntax, 61 focused tests,\n  187 server files/1,489 tests, and `build:app`; this is not represented as a\n  canonical final-parent run.\n- Changed release notes in the reconstructed series pass the forbidden-term\n  scan and use plain product language.\n\n### Pending final-tree evidence\n\n- Create positions 95-99, then prove exactly 99 first-parent commits and one\n  intended local/remote branch per position with no 100th branch.\n- Run the repository's complete canonical local-first gate at every final\n  branch head before pushing or proposing that branch. Focused runs and one\n  green integrated tip do not satisfy this per-head requirement.\n- On the unchanged final integrated tree, complete release validation, format,\n  lint, full Angular and server suites, production build, infrastructure checks,\n  and image-security verification.\n- Run the complete PostgreSQL 17 integration project, including event-role,\n  registration/payment/transfer, tenant, receipt, and email concurrency proof.\n- Run the complete credentialed functional, generated-guide, integration, and\n  live-provider release commands with zero incomplete outcomes; then audit and\n  build the exact Pages output and inspect the neutral crop.\n- Exercise real project-scoped Docker start, stop, status, resume, teardown,\n  readiness, and empty-volume behavior after the bounded layer; do not use a\n  second stack or retry as fallback evidence.\n- Perform branch-authentic Codex Browser acceptance separately from Playwright\n  for anonymous/direct-link discovery, participant flows, organizer/scanner,\n  tenant finance/settings, and platform administration. If Browser control is\n  unavailable, record the blocker instead of substituting screenshots or\n  system Chrome.\n\n### Former reference-tree evidence (preserved provenance only)\n\nEverything below this subheading was collected on the superseded reference\ntree. Words such as “current” and “final” are retained as historical record and\nmust not be read as proof for the reconstructed 99-layer stack.\n\n- Legacy deletion source/schema guards: 31/31 and 23/23.\n- Fresh-schema tenant/permission/settings server tests: 86/86.\n- Fresh-schema Angular/shared tests: 54/54.\n- D-003 focused proof covers signed-in option-derived discovery, anonymous\n  default-role discovery through the public projection, sign-in before\n  registration, server-side eligibility rechecks, explicit direct-link\n  ineligibility, deletion of event/template audience state, template structural\n  snapshots, and the separate announcement-role rule.\n- Event/provider fail-loud Angular tests: 92/92.\n- Check-in handler tests: 96/96.\n- Auth/config tests: 14/14; SSR cookie forwarding: 9/9.\n- Auth request-origin and inbound-boundary tests: 20/20.\n- RPC ingress tests: 22/22; SSR/client integration: 15/15.\n- Typed RPC request-context, user-handler, and request-resolver tests: 37/37.\n- Members Hub/onboarding/permission-guard Angular tests: 12/12.\n- Tax-label/dead-helper focused server and Angular tests: 10/10.\n- Registration seed/auth-account helper tests: 14/14; affected Playwright\n  dependency/test collection: 9/9.\n- Platform audit, check-in, and platform-registration server tests: 145/145.\n- Scanner, platform audit, profile-query gating, role/tax/icon, event-list, and\n  shared-contract Angular tests: 101/101.\n- Admin settings/overview/user-list Angular tests: 20/20.\n- Identity, admin, list-contract, and audit server tests: 96/96.\n- Identity/admin list and provider-state Angular/shared tests: 72/72.\n- SSR origin and server configuration initialization Angular tests: 9/9.\n- Rich-text sanitizer tests: 4/4; affected rich-text form schema tests: 26/26.\n- Event-list identity contract tests: 29/29 server and 2/2 Angular.\n- Event creation/query integrity tests: 31/31 server; event route, review,\n  details, and paged-list tests: 40/40 Angular.\n- Registration snapshot, question-history, check-in, handler, platform, and\n  serialization tests: 178/178.\n- Database ownership, privacy-version, request-context, onboarding, global\n  administration, and seed-prerequisite tests: 67/67.\n- Strict tenant/receipt/provider configuration tests: 22/22.\n- Profile email and payout validation tests: 31/31.\n- `tsc -p tsconfig.app.json --noEmit` passed after the database, privacy, and\n  seed changes.\n- Test discovery, skip inventory, storage-state, and suite-ownership tests:\n  29/29; current functional Playwright baseline: 153/153.\n- The current functional baseline surfaced one lost pre-readiness tax-rate\n  import click. The focused fix waits for the existing readiness marker and\n  clicks once; the 153/153 rerun has no click retry, delay, skip, or fallback.\n- Receipt storage/finance handler tests: 71/71.\n- Finance lifecycle, schema, platform reimbursement, and audit tests: 88/88;\n  receipt value/date/reimbursement contract tests: 53/53.\n- Finance shared-policy, receipt UI, event-organizer, and platform-finance\n  Angular tests: 81/81.\n- Receipt detail/list-contract Angular tests: 33/33.\n- Security boundary tests: 51 focused server tests plus cache/telemetry tests.\n- Infrastructure/source tests: 37/37.\n- Terraform validation passed for bootstrap, production, and staging.\n- `bun run infra:check`: the first provider download received a GitHub 504;\n  the exact unchanged retry passed all three Terraform roots and reported zero\n  Trivy misconfigurations.\n- `bun run release:validate` passed.\n- Multiple focused `bun run lint`, `bun run format:write`,\n  `bun run build:app`, and `git diff --check` runs passed.\n- Integrated `tsc -p tsconfig.app.json --noEmit` and\n  `tsc -p tsconfig.spec.json --noEmit` passed.\n- Integrated `bun run format:check`, `bun run lint`, and\n  `bun run build:app` passed.\n- Integrated Angular suite: 144 files, 1,106 tests passed.\n- Integrated server suite: 199 files, 1,603 tests passed.\n- Current request-boundary, request-body, worker-route, and server-response\n  regressions: 36/36.\n- Current event registration handler regressions: 101/101.\n- Current global-administration handler regressions: 21/21, including complete\n  and incomplete sent email records.\n- Current Angular application/configuration and event-identity regressions:\n  36/36.\n- Default/classic/ESN theme schema and focused administration/form tests: 3/3\n  and 47/47; all three compiled light/dark theme classes were exercised in\n  Chromium, including Material primary, primary-container, tertiary, and\n  surface role contrast plus exact standard/high-contrast primary values; both\n  palette generator commands reproduce their tracked files.\n- PostgreSQL integration: 17 files, 83/83 tests passed after explicitly\n  restarting the worktree stack removed by Playwright. The first\n  `ECONNREFUSED` was environmental disposal, not a test retry; the exact same\n  command passed without timeout or fallback changes, and `evorto-cda27261`\n  remained untouched. Persistent and disposable stacks are now run in sequence:\n  stop the persistent stack before Playwright, then recreate it for PostgreSQL.\n- Settled-decision focused server tests: waitlist, transfer, combined Checkout,\n  settings validation, announcement discovery, and profile routing passed\n  without skips or retries.\n- Settled-decision focused PostgreSQL tests prove active-limit conversion,\n  fixed-bundle payment finalization, role-targeted announcement discovery,\n  role-deletion integrity, and the platform-update versus role-delete race.\n- Settled-decision focused Angular/shared tests cover the five settings pages,\n  routed profile ownership, tenant-admin/platform-admin announcement role selection,\n  explicit permissions, and current documentation contracts.\n- Final decision follow-up tests: checkout amount boundaries 67/67; payment\n  account handlers 71/71; provider failure classification 4/4; payment\n  contracts/forms 45/45; focused settings guard/hydration 33/33. The\n  tenant-admin announcement dialog now has behavioral role-catalog and mutation-failure\n  coverage, and the routed profile shell has explicit focus-contract coverage.\n- Focused settings hydration/readiness tests: 18/18.\n- Current `image:security:local` gate: the 95,726,857-byte linux/amd64 runtime\n  image contains no source maps; private maps were exported separately. SBOM\n  generation, runtime verification, and the dependency scan passed with zero\n  vulnerabilities. An earlier overlapping image/application build exhausted\n  Docker memory and exited 137 before producing a usable result; the passing\n  evidence is the later isolated unchanged rerun, not a hidden retry or code\n  fix. The separately user-cancelled repository scan was not restarted.\n- Rebuilt isolated distroless stack: web `/readyz` returned HTTP 204; Bun ran as\n  PID 1, and the worker started both polling loops without a shell or command\n  override.\n- Theme Playwright smoke: database setup plus the selected theme scenario\n  passed 2/2. Default, Classic, and ESN Material primary,\n  primary-container, tertiary, and surface roles meet their standard and\n  increased-contrast requirements across light and dark modes.\n- Representative PostgreSQL planning: four read-only `EXPLAIN` statements\n  completed and rolled back; current indexes were selected where the seeded\n  cardinality was meaningful, and no speculative index was added.\n- Rebuilt container `/readyz`: HTTP 204.\n- Authenticated Playwright setup: database setup and all six real Auth0 account\n  logins passed through the isolated runner.\n- Current credential-backed functional Playwright suite: 153/153 passed through real\n  Auth0 with zero failures, skips, retries, or incomplete tests.\n- Current credential-backed integration Playwright suite: 11/11 passed with\n  zero failures, skips, retries, or incomplete tests.\n- Current corrected provider-backed documentation publication: 54/54 passed\n  with zero failures, skips, retries, or incomplete tests and copied the exact\n  13-guide, 199-asset catalog.\n- Current live ESNcard release certification: 8 focused unit checks and all 9\n  provider-backed Playwright journeys passed. The functional journey waits for\n  hydration, polls the persisted card status, and proves that `lastCheckedAt`\n  advances; no cache workaround, retry, or fallback remains.\n- Current published documentation audit: the exact 13-guide catalog contains\n  199 PNG assets and 203 references to all 199 assets, with zero missing or\n  unused files. The first-steps image shows only the neutral, editable\n  `person@example.org` email step; its exact crop was visually inspected. The\n  publication guard rejected visible loading copy, and the Pages tooling found\n  no internal product wording in authored or rendered guide copy.\n- Companion Pages [PR #15](https://github.com/heddendorp/evorto/pull/15) passes\n  19/19 documentation-tooling tests, lint, `git diff --check`, and a 23-page\n  production build. All 13 current destinations are present and the five\n  retired content and asset destinations are absent; no publication blocker\n  remains.\n- Interactive Browser acceptance: the branch-authentic anonymous event list\n  exposed option-derived published events. Opening Small Event Example 2 showed\n  only the public projection plus “Sign in before signing up” and the “Sign in\n  now” action. The active root theme was `theme-evorto`, and the computed\n  Material primary, secondary, tertiary, neutral, and error roles matched the\n  new default palette in light/dark form. Browser logs were empty.\n\n## Completion state\n\nThe source review is closed at the position-94 checkpoint: all 157 findings\nhave an implementation outcome, 155 are resolved, 2 are accepted at explicit\nboundaries, all 41 simplification candidates retain a concrete deletion test or\naccepted boundary, and D-001 through D-008 remain settled. The corrected\nRQ-002/RQ-004, F-020, C-037, D-003, and D-004 event direction is preserved.\n\nFinal verification is **in progress**, not complete. RQ-003 through RQ-012\nretain the exact environment gates named in the reconstructed coverage table,\nand RQ-015 remains open until all 99 final heads and the unchanged integrated\ntip satisfy the pending evidence list. Historical PostgreSQL, provider,\npublication, image, Pages, and Browser counts are provenance only.\n\nCompletion requires:\n\n- the one-file position-95 patch and four prepared latency layers to produce\n  exactly 99 first-parent commits with no empty, fixup, temporary, or 100th\n  layer;\n- every final branch to pass its complete local PR-equivalent gate before any\n  push or proposal that can trigger CI;\n- every final integrated environment gate to pass without failures, skips,\n  todos, fixmes, expected failures, retries/flakes, interruptions, focused\n  selection, hidden fallback, or compatibility substitution;\n- Browser acceptance, or its exact control-transport blocker, to remain\n  separate from Playwright and screenshot evidence; and\n- final commit/tree, branch, test-count, runtime, and publication evidence to\n  be recorded from the actual final stack rather than copied from this\n  pre-position-95 checkpoint.\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T05:44:38.761Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-a949d200-08e8-4217-b274-bb38bf16ddee","turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Application Review Queue\n\nUpdated: 2026-08-05\n\nReview branch: `codex/full-application-simplification-review`\n\nReview baseline: latest fetched `origin/main` at\n`d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea` (verified 2026-08-05)\n\n## Reconstructed stack checkpoint\n\nThis queue is prepared against the exact position-94 commit\n`571e511252bc2d03ddcf385ac34d2ebbfdd308d9`, tree\n`dfad7e748ff9f8b23698c8263bf4eb90b07c5aba`. It records the intended final\n99-layer stack shape without inventing a position-95 or final position-99\ncommit. Those commits do not exist until this one-file queue patch and the four\nprepared staging-latency patches are applied.\n\n| Positions | Scope                                                                          | Current checkpoint                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1-80      | Reconstructed application source                                               | Exact 80-layer prefix ending at `bf29eb4a8b990e115c8819a76b110b90e50d8e86`; every layer has one intended branch and satisfies the review-size rules, including the sole approved one-file generated-snapshot deletion |\n| 81        | Platform administration contracts                                              | `d47f6ec9cee2cdbbdc05187286994dd08d007936`, tree `7a7a4e1bbb3bca365c8cc8d72a8ddb7c711ba7cb`                                                                                                                           |\n| 82-93     | UI, generated guides, and acceptance guards                                    | Exact 12-layer replay ending at `b7d92dacd4d64d0bde2c96e083612e20ac123ef6`, tree `4c55b1f629b60d2c4603ff6d2168ec24a1f026eb`                                                                                           |\n| 94        | Bounded local Docker lifecycle                                                 | `571e511252bc2d03ddcf385ac34d2ebbfdd308d9`, tree `dfad7e748ff9f8b23698c8263bf4eb90b07c5aba`                                                                                                                           |\n| 95        | This review queue                                                              | One new file only; commit and tree intentionally remain unrecorded until the patch is applied                                                                                                                         |\n| 96-99     | Request tracing, bounded staging probe, automated evidence, and response guide | Four focused patches are prepared and replay cleanly after the position-94 tree; their final shared commits must be created only after position 95                                                                    |\n\nExactly 99 layers are planned. A 100th layer, an empty/fixup layer, or a final\nSHA copied from a provisional replay would violate this checkpoint.\n\n## Objective\n\nReview the complete application and leave it safe, direct, and maintainable by\none developer. Find and resolve bugs, inconsistencies, missing implementation,\nsecurity defects, unnecessary complexity, hidden failures, ambitious\nfallbacks, and backwards-compatibility code.\n\nThe finished project will be deployed from a fresh schema. Historical data\nimport and compatibility behavior are not product requirements.\n\n## Review rules\n\n- Prefer one obvious implementation over layered compatibility paths.\n- Surface unexpected failures; do not turn defects into plausible-looking\n  fallback results.\n- Keep only complexity required by a documented product invariant.\n- Enforce tenant, identity, permission, payment, and file boundaries on the\n  server.\n- Keep external side effects explicit. An ambiguous payment or email outcome\n  must stop for review rather than retry automatically.\n- Use defaults only when creating new records. Invalid persisted state must\n  fail decoding or validation.\n- Verify user-facing behavior through normal navigation and durable tests.\n- A queue item closes only with current source or runtime evidence.\n\n## Status definitions\n\n- **Resolved**: implementation and focused verification are complete.\n- **In progress**: a bounded implementation batch is active or awaiting its\n  integrated verification.\n- **Open**: validated and not yet implemented.\n- **Decision**: the code cannot be simplified safely until the named product\n  choice is made.\n- **Accepted**: complexity is justified by a documented invariant and has a\n  recorded boundary.\n- **In progress** (coverage): the review is complete, but one or more named\n  current-tree verification gates are still running.\n- **Complete** (coverage): the required review and its current evidence are\n  complete.\n- **Blocked** (coverage): an exact named external prerequisite prevents the\n  required evidence; weaker evidence is not substituted.\n\n## Reconstructed coverage queue\n\n`Complete` below means the current reconstruction has enough source and\ndatabase-free evidence to close that review area. `In progress` names the\nremaining final-tree environment or canonical-suite proof explicitly; earlier\nevidence is not substituted.\n\n| ID     | Current status | Current reconstruction evidence                                                                                                                                                                     | Still required                                                                                                                                |\n| ------ | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| RQ-001 | Complete       | Historical ledgers, the legacy importer and schema tree, migration-only tests, and obsolete deployment-data scripts remain deleted in the reconstructed prefix                                      | Confirm the same deletions in the final 99-layer diff                                                                                         |\n| RQ-002 | Complete       | PRODUCT.md and ARCHITECTURE.md match sign-up-derived ordinary discovery, structural templates, and separately role-targeted announcements; the misleading unused public-event capability is deleted | Confirm the final four layers do not alter these boundaries                                                                                   |\n| RQ-003 | In progress    | SSR, request-boundary, identity, settings, and administration source plus database-free tests are reconstructed                                                                                     | Canonical final-head suites and branch-authentic Browser SSR/hydration acceptance                                                             |\n| RQ-004 | In progress    | D-003 and D-004 source, UI, direct-link outcomes, generated-guide sources, and stale-model deletions are reconstructed                                                                              | Final PostgreSQL, credentialed journey, generated-guide, and Browser proof                                                                    |\n| RQ-005 | In progress    | Registration, eligibility, capacity, questions, add-ons, waitlists, check-in, and cancellation behavior has source and focused-test evidence                                                        | Final PostgreSQL concurrency and complete functional journeys                                                                                 |\n| RQ-006 | In progress    | Transfer, checkout, payment ownership, attachment, refund, and paid-access behavior has source and focused-test evidence                                                                            | Final PostgreSQL plus credentialed payment and transfer journeys                                                                              |\n| RQ-007 | In progress    | Identity, role, settings, tenant, and platform-administration boundaries are reconstructed with typed focused coverage                                                                              | Final Auth0-backed administration journeys and Browser acceptance                                                                             |\n| RQ-008 | In progress    | Receipt, reimbursement, object-storage, email-outbox, worker, and failure-visibility behavior has source and database-free proof                                                                    | Final receipt/email PostgreSQL tests and credentialed finance journeys                                                                        |\n| RQ-009 | In progress    | Request boundaries, typed failures, trace context, workers, and fail-visible behavior are reconstructed                                                                                             | Canonical unfiltered final-head server/unit/build gates                                                                                       |\n| RQ-010 | In progress    | Fresh-schema persistence shapes, constraints, tenant locks, and ledgers are source-reviewed                                                                                                         | Complete PostgreSQL 17 integration suite and any retained read-only planning checks                                                           |\n| RQ-011 | In progress    | Position 94 bounds every ordinary Compose operation, reports project state, and removes teardown retry behavior; shell syntax and 45 focused Vitest tests pass                                      | Real project-scoped start/stop/status/resume/readiness, infrastructure validation, and image-security proof on the unchanged final tree       |\n| RQ-012 | In progress    | The exact 12-layer UI/docs series passes 134 Angular files/966 tests, 187 server files/1,497 tests, build, format, lint, diff, wording, and active-skip guards                                      | Credentialed functional/integration/provider documentation publication, exact Pages audit/build, and visual crop inspection on the final tree |\n| RQ-013 | Complete       | Manual security review outcomes remain recorded; the user-cancelled automated scan is explicitly not represented as completed                                                                       | No scan restart is required by this reconstruction                                                                                            |\n| RQ-014 | Complete       | All 41 simplification candidates and their deletion tests or accepted boundaries remain recorded                                                                                                    | Confirm the final latency layers add no fallback or compatibility surface                                                                     |\n| RQ-015 | In progress    | The exact 94-layer executable/documentation prefix is structurally assembled; UI full suites and the final Docker focused suite are green                                                           | Apply positions 95-99, audit exactly 99 heads, then complete every canonical per-head and final integrated environment gate listed below      |\n\n### Historical reference coverage snapshot\n\nThe table below is retained as provenance from the former reference tree. Its\n`Complete` cells and counts are not current proof for the reconstructed stack;\nthe authoritative status is the table above.\n\n| ID     | Area                        | Required manual review                                                                 | Status   | Evidence                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------ | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| RQ-001 | Historical artifacts        | Obsolete scan/compliance output and stale references                                   | Complete | Historical compliance ledger, legacy importer, old schema tree, migration-only tests, and two deployment-data audit scripts identified and removed                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| RQ-002 | Product and architecture    | Implemented workflows against PRODUCT.md and ARCHITECTURE.md                           | Complete | D-003 is implemented end to end: ordinary discovery derives from current sign-up eligibility, templates carry structure only, and announcements retain their separate selected-role rule                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| RQ-003 | App shell and SSR           | Routing, hydration, auth state, tenant resolution, navigation, error states            | Complete | Manual source/test review plus focused SSR and request-boundary tests                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| RQ-004 | Events and templates        | Authoring, review, publishing, discovery, snapshots, eligibility                       | Complete | Obsolete ordinary event/template audience state and controls are deleted; server, UI, schema, public view, direct-link, and structural-snapshot behavior implement D-003                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| RQ-005 | Registration operations     | Eligibility, capacity, questions, add-ons, waitlists, check-in                         | Complete | Registration handlers/services and concurrency paths traced                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| RQ-006 | Transfers and payments      | Fixed-bundle transfer, checkout, webhooks, refunds, Stripe ownership                   | Complete | Checkout, webhook, transfer, acquisition, and refund paths traced                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| RQ-007 | Identity and administration | Onboarding, roles, capabilities, tenant settings, platform authority, audit trail      | Complete | Auth0, request context, regular/platform administration, and audit paths traced                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| RQ-008 | Finance and notifications   | Receipts, storage, reimbursements, email outbox, failure visibility                    | Complete | Tenant/platform finance, object storage, outbox, provider, and worker paths traced                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| RQ-009 | Server and RPC              | Contracts, typed errors, defects, retries, fallbacks, concurrency, observability       | Complete | Bun/Node adapters, Effect RPC ingress, error schemas, logs, and traces traced                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| RQ-010 | Database                    | Schema invariants, constraints, query isolation, obsolete migration state              | Complete | Drizzle schema and key transactional services reviewed against fresh-schema requirements                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| RQ-011 | Operations                  | Configuration, secrets, Docker, workers, deployment, health/readiness                  | Complete | CI, seed helpers, Docker, Scaleway, Terraform, and release workflows traced                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| RQ-012 | Tests and documentation     | Missing behavior, hidden skips, weak assertions, stale generated docs                  | Complete | The corrected official provider-backed publication passed 54/54 without failures, skips, retries, or incomplete tests and transactionally replaced both tracked Pages destinations with the exact 13-guide catalog and 199 assets. The published guides contain 203 references to all 199 assets, with zero missing or unused files; all five retired guide content and asset paths are absent. The exact neutral first-steps email crop was visually inspected. The Pages branch passes 19/19 publication-tooling tests, plain-language checks, lint, `git diff --check`, and its 23-page production build. No generated-page patch, compatibility alias, partial bundle, or stale output was substituted. |\n| RQ-013 | Manual security review      | Authn/authz, tenant isolation, CSRF, XSS, uploads, redirects, SSR leakage              | Complete | Manual review only; scan workers and temporary output were stopped and removed, while durable cancellation acknowledgment was blocked by the scan service                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| RQ-014 | Simplification review       | Shallow modules, duplicated policy, speculative seams, deletion opportunities          | Complete | Candidates and concrete simpler directions recorded below                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| RQ-015 | Final verification          | Lint, format, build, unit, integration, image security, Playwright, Browser acceptance | Complete | Frozen local install, format, lint, both explicit type checks, production build, release validation, Terraform bootstrap/production/staging with zero misconfigurations, 144-file/1,106-test Angular, 199-file/1,603-test server, 17-file/83-test PostgreSQL, 153/153 functional, 11/11 integration, 54/54 provider-backed guide publication, 8-focused-unit-check/9-journey live ESNcard certification, verified Pages output, and branch-authentic Browser checks pass. The 95,726,857-byte linux/amd64 runtime image contains no source maps; they were exported separately, and the final image check found zero vulnerabilities. The user-cancelled repository scan was not restarted.                 |\n\n## Findings queue\n\nCurrent totals: **157 findings** — 1 Critical, 53 High, 89 Medium, and 14\nLow. **155 are resolved and 2 are accepted with explicit boundaries. No finding\nawaits a product decision.**\n\nFinding outcomes describe the implementation state. Final environment evidence\nis tracked separately in the reconstructed coverage queue and must not be\ninferred from historical wording such as “current tree” in the preserved\nreference evidence.\n\n### Critical boundaries\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                                           | Required simple outcome                                                                                                   | Status   |\n| ----- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| F-001 | Critical | Staging and production were conditionally reconciled from one Terraform root/state; a staging apply could plan production destruction          | Unconditional per-environment roots, state and credentials; no counts, targets, moved blocks, or cross-environment inputs | Resolved |\n| F-002 | High     | Transfer bearer credentials were embedded in `/registration-transfers/:credential`, OAuth redirects, logs, traces, and referrers               | Keep one hashed manual claim code, use a generic route, and submit the code only in the RPC body                          | Resolved |\n| F-003 | High     | Email `sending` leases could be reclaimed after provider acceptance and resend the same message; the custom header is not provider idempotency | Dispatch only `queued`; make stale/ambiguous delivery terminal; deadline before lease; no automatic ambiguous retry       | Resolved |\n| F-004 | High     | Public RPC error schemas carry `Schema.Defect` causes that can serialize SQL, parameters, PII, and stack detail                                | Public errors carry safe typed data only; log a redacted internal diagnostic with request ID                              | Resolved |\n| F-005 | High     | Receipt storage HEAD/signing failures were converted into missing evidence or preview-unavailable results                                      | Preserve a typed service-unavailable outcome; only confirmed not-found means missing evidence                             | Resolved |\n\n### Security, identity, and request handling\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                                                                                  | Required simple outcome                                                                                                                                               | Status   |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| F-006 | High     | Cookie-authenticated `/rpc` accepted arbitrary content types and sibling-subdomain origins                                                                                            | Exact JSON and same-origin before auth/body decoding, with one proved loopback SSR exception                                                                          | Resolved |\n| F-007 | High     | Production Bun traffic bypassed the Node Host/forwarded-protocol trust boundary                                                                                                       | One inbound normalizer shared by both adapters; no deprecated or untrusted forwarded-header fallback                                                                  | Resolved |\n| F-008 | High     | Auth0 accepted weak secrets and malformed origins; cookie identifiers/deletion did not match the SDK; logout/provider fallbacks hid failures                                          | Strict redacted config, explicit cookies, hosted Secure flags, and visible provider failures                                                                          | Resolved |\n| F-009 | High     | `icons.add` treated ambient platform authority as tenant permission without explicit target/reason/audit                                                                              | Regular RPC requires tenant permission; add no platform bypass unless a real caller needs a dedicated audited operation                                               | Resolved |\n| F-010 | High     | Members Hub route and `admin.roles.findHubRoles` exposed tenant member names without `internal:viewInternalPages`                                                                     | Enforce the capability in both the route and server handler                                                                                                           | Resolved |\n| F-011 | Medium   | Default HTTP logging and raw `request.url` trace fields captured credentials and callback queries                                                                                     | Disable raw request logger; trace sanitized route templates only                                                                                                      | Resolved |\n| F-012 | Medium   | Dynamic SSR and authenticated QR responses lacked explicit private no-store caching                                                                                                   | `private, no-store` on dynamic/authenticated output; immutable assets remain cacheable                                                                                | Resolved |\n| F-013 | Medium   | Browser telemetry silently dropped oversized errors and used a process-global quota/fingerprint                                                                                       | Bound fields, redact credentials, include path, and isolate bounded state per trusted host                                                                            | Resolved |\n| F-014 | Medium   | E2E platform-admin authority was derived from process environment with only a `NODE_ENV` gate                                                                                         | Test-only injection; hosted startup rejects E2E authority variables                                                                                                   | Resolved |\n| F-015 | Medium   | Onboarding status returned `{complete:false}` when the authenticated claim lacked `sub`                                                                                               | Return the same explicit unauthorized outcome as the requirements endpoint                                                                                            | Resolved |\n| F-016 | Medium   | Onboarding completion left the client-side permission/request context stale until reload                                                                                              | Full document navigation after success                                                                                                                                | Resolved |\n| F-078 | High     | Tenant brand-asset upload trusted the claimed image MIME type and served arbitrary bytes from the application origin                                                                  | Verify PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, or ICO signatures before storage; reject a MIME mismatch                                                                                 | Resolved |\n| F-074 | High     | Auth0 `globalAdmin` app metadata remained an undocumented backwards-compatible platform-authority alias                                                                               | Accept only the canonical `platformAdministrator` authority key                                                                                                       | Resolved |\n| F-077 | High     | Tenant role reads silently discarded persisted platform-global permissions and hid corrupt authority data                                                                             | Strictly decode tenant-only role permissions at the first read boundary and fail loudly                                                                               | Resolved |\n| F-079 | Medium   | Public approved-event responses exposed reviewer identity and internal review comments                                                                                                | Keep public event projections free of private review metadata; expose it only through an authorized operation                                                         | Resolved |\n| F-081 | Medium   | SSR RPC/config initialization could continue with a hard-coded localhost origin or without request context                                                                            | Require one valid request/configured origin and server request context; fail startup/render visibly                                                                   | Resolved |\n| F-082 | Medium   | Rich-text mounted an image subsystem with no uploader while allowing third-party tracking images and showing impossible upload guidance                                               | Remove image support and blob-upload state until an owned upload product flow exists                                                                                  | Resolved |\n| F-085 | Medium   | Auth request-origin resolution retained a deprecated forwarded-protocol alias and invented a localhost origin when normalized context was absent                                      | Accept only normalized protocol and required Host; fail visibly when the inbound boundary was not established                                                         | Resolved |\n| F-088 | Medium   | Event identity failures were treated as anonymous, personal-card queries ran without confirmed identity, and cached identity could retain creator controls after a failed refresh     | Render an explicit identity retry and gate creator, organizer, and personal-card queries and cached data on a successful authenticated identity result                | Resolved |\n| F-089 | Medium   | Angular route discovery checked its no-request lifecycle only after constructing `ConfigService` and its request-bound RPC/query dependencies                                         | Check the official route-discovery token in the app initializer before injecting `ConfigService`; real SSR still requires request context                             | Resolved |\n| F-095 | Medium   | Accepted tenant configuration did not directly apply its document theme class, while `index.html` advertised two static browser colors that matched none of the available palettes    | Apply exactly one current theme class through the shared tenant-configuration path and delete the invalid static `theme-color` tags; add no dynamic mapping subsystem | Resolved |\n| F-090 | High     | Direct TLS requests normalized by the Node adapter traversed the global boundary again and were downgraded to HTTP when platform proxy trust was disabled                             | Apply the inbound boundary exactly once: Node uses its normalized request, while Bun retains the ingress boundary; prove direct TLS and spoof rejection               | Resolved |\n| F-092 | High     | Distributed request rebuilding transferred Bun's streaming body to a different Web `Request`, leaving the downstream RPC request body-used and making accepted POST bodies unreadable | Rebuild once inside the boundary middleware, provide that normalized server request downstream, and prove an accepted RPC POST body remains readable                  | Resolved |\n| F-017 | Medium   | Regular user/event/finance list contracts accept negative, fractional, or unbounded paging and invalid dates                                                                          | One bounded integer page schema (maximum 100) and strict date inputs                                                                                                  | Resolved |\n| F-018 | Medium   | Platform audit history is hard-limited to 100 and the UI hides IDs/permissions needed to understand authority changes                                                                 | Cursor pagination and visible safe authority fields                                                                                                                   | Resolved |\n\n### Events, templates, and registration\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Required simple outcome                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Status                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| F-019 | High     | Ongoing events disappear at their start because discovery filters by `start > now`                                                                                                                                                    | Discover while `end > from`                                                                                                                                                                                               | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-020 | High     | Ordinary events and templates store a separately configured participant/organizer/both/unlisted audience, duplicating sign-up eligibility and allowing discovery to drift from who can actually sign up                               | Delete ordinary event and template audience state; derive signed-in discovery from current sign-up eligibility and anonymous discovery from choices available to default roles, while rechecking every registration write | Resolved: the audience state, contracts, controls, seed state, and compatibility paths are deleted; discovery and every registration boundary now use current eligibility |\n| F-021 | High     | Template/event authoring can silently drop ESN discounts or zero a paid graph when provider/Stripe capability is unavailable                                                                                                          | Block the write with a typed unavailable result and preserve pricing                                                                                                                                                      | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-022 | High     | Capability, discount, tax, role, and icon query failures were mapped to `false`, `{}`, or empty lists                                                                                                                                 | Distinguish unavailable from disabled/empty and show an actionable error                                                                                                                                                  | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-023 | High     | Check-in validated mutable owner/status/guest state before the lock and returned invented success after races                                                                                                                         | Lock and reread all mutable state; only persisted exact retries are idempotent                                                                                                                                            | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-024 | Medium   | Check-in remains open indefinitely after an event                                                                                                                                                                                     | Close at event end plus one explicit grace period and return an ended reason                                                                                                                                              | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-025 | High     | Retrying `registerForEvent` can ignore changed guests, answers, or add-ons and resume an older Checkout                                                                                                                               | Separate choice-free retry operation; reject an active existing registration from normal create                                                                                                                           | Resolved: normal create rejects active state; an owned choice-free RPC/UI retry resumes only persisted terms                                                              |\n| F-026 | High     | Guest/add-on quantities are unbounded and feed an O(n) refund allocator; valid graphs can exceed Stripe's 100 line-item limit                                                                                                         | Small product caps at UI/contract/service/DB boundaries plus a pre-reservation line-count check                                                                                                                           | Resolved: 10 guests, 10 units per add-on, 20 add-on types, and a 100-line pre-reservation Checkout guard                                                                  |\n| F-027 | Medium   | Checkout cleanup discards reschedule failures with `Effect.ignore` and reports only aggregates                                                                                                                                        | Propagate or aggregate identified failures; no clean-looking result after partial failure                                                                                                                                 | Resolved: registration and add-on reschedule persistence failures now fail the worker iteration visibly                                                                   |\n| F-028 | High     | Confirmed/payment-pending registrations can lack price snapshots and views reconstruct history from mutable prices or zero                                                                                                            | Require immutable snapshots, store explicit zero for free confirmations, and delete reconstruction fallbacks                                                                                                              | Resolved: writers persist complete snapshots, DB checks enforce them, and reads fail on missing history                                                                   |\n| F-029 | Medium   | Current Stripe sessions always write metadata but completion accepts metadata-free historical sessions                                                                                                                                | Require the exact current metadata tuple; delete compatibility branches/fixtures                                                                                                                                          | Resolved: completion accepts only the exact current registration, tenant, transaction, and transfer tuple                                                                 |\n| F-030 | Medium   | Questions/answers lack pragmatic size/count limits and duplicate answers can overwrite silently                                                                                                                                       | Bounded inputs and explicit duplicate rejection                                                                                                                                                                           | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-031 | Medium   | Scanner opens the camera before capability resolution and can stop permanently after navigation failure                                                                                                                               | Resolve capability first; surface navigation failure and restore an explicit retry state                                                                                                                                  | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-032 | Medium   | Listing/filter/paging UI contains no-op controls, hidden mutation failures, and a fixed first 100                                                                                                                                     | Delete controls with no product behavior or implement URL state and load-more; show mutation failures                                                                                                                     | Resolved: dead controls deleted; bounded deterministic load-more preserves prior pages and exposes failures                                                               |\n| F-071 | High     | Platform event editing could change title, description, requiredness, order, or option ownership after answers existed                                                                                                                | Share the ordinary immutable-after-answer guard with platform editing; no historical-answer rewrite                                                                                                                       | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-075 | Medium   | Event option policy inheritance could be inferred from omitted write fields                                                                                                                                                           | Require an explicit null or override value; keep omitted policy state invalid                                                                                                                                             | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-076 | Medium   | Template reads silently dropped unresolved role IDs even though the array cannot have a database foreign key                                                                                                                          | Treat an unresolved persisted role as an integrity defect with template, option, and role context                                                                                                                         | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-080 | Medium   | Event edit/organizer route guards converted transport, authorization, decoding, and server failures into false 404s                                                                                                                   | Route only true not-found to 404, handle explicit auth outcomes, and surface unexpected unavailability                                                                                                                    | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-083 | Low      | Event review recovery branched on English message substrings despite tagged RPC errors                                                                                                                                                | Switch on the decoded error tag and delete copy-dependent heuristics                                                                                                                                                      | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-084 | Low      | Event-list `userId` and a `users.maybeSelf` request duplicated identity already held by authenticated server context                                                                                                                  | Delete the input, mismatch warning, and extra identity query                                                                                                                                                              | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-086 | High     | Event creation positionally matched returned option rows and silently filtered add-on mappings when persistence returned an incomplete/reordered set                                                                                  | Pre-generate option IDs and require every declared discount, add-on, and question mapping                                                                                                                                 | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-087 | Medium   | Anonymous event details invoked the authenticated organizer-capability RPC and rendered its authorization failure as a public-page outage                                                                                             | Enable the capability query only after `maybeSelf` confirms authentication; never expose cached organizer state anonymously                                                                                               | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-091 | Medium   | Registration-transfer tests still modeled the deleted recipient-registration column, ignored the fresh source/status/tenant predicate, omitted refund-stage new-transfer coverage, and suggested cancellation where it is unavailable | Test only the fresh source-registration model, prove refund-stage preview and commit remain blocked without mutation, and use stage-neutral recovery guidance                                                             | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                  |\n\n### Finance and notifications\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                               | Required simple outcome                                                                          | Status                                                                                   |\n| ----- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| F-033 | High     | Receipt amounts are arbitrary numbers, contradictory values are silently zeroed, and zero totals can enter an unreimbursable state | Positive integer minor units; reject precision/contradictions; bounded paging                    | Resolved: one strict minor-unit policy now spans RPC, UI, handlers, and database checks  |\n| F-034 | High     | Receipt calendar dates are stored/transported as timestamps and can shift day by timezone                                          | PostgreSQL `date` and strict `YYYY-MM-DD` end to end                                             | Resolved: calendar dates remain strict strings over a PostgreSQL `date` column           |\n| F-035 | High     | Tenant reimbursement is an irreversible one-click mutation while platform reimbursement has a clear confirmation                   | Reuse one confirmation model and cap each batch at 100                                           | Resolved: both paths use one confirmation dialog and one shared 100-receipt limit        |\n| F-036 | High     | Platform finance UI replaces actionable typed failures with generic catch messages                                                 | Render typed conflict, ambiguity, review, and storage outcomes                                   | Resolved: all platform finance mutation catches render decoded typed messages            |\n| F-037 | High     | Concurrent upload finalization performs repeated 20 MiB download/hash/upload work before one conditional write wins                | Atomically claim `pending -> finalizing`; interrupted work is terminal and the user starts fresh | Resolved: only the atomic claim winner performs storage inspection                       |\n| F-038 | High     | Orphan cleanup holds DB locks during remote storage work and can roll back DB state after irreversible object deletion             | Brief claims and independent per-row processing; normalized not-found only                       | Resolved: brief `cleaning` claims precede independent remote and row deletion            |\n| F-039 | Medium   | Reimbursement audit does not retain the immutable payout fingerprint/masked destination confirmed by the operator                  | Persist fingerprint and safe masked destination in the reimbursement audit                       | Resolved: audit state stores the validated SHA-256 fingerprint and masked destination    |\n| F-040 | Medium   | Browser receipt file acceptance disagrees with server MIME/20 MiB rules                                                            | Share one MIME/size contract and reject before upload                                            | Resolved: browser and server consume one exact MIME and size validator                   |\n| F-041 | Medium   | Receipt-country configuration drops invalid entries and substitutes defaults for invalid persisted state                           | Validate nonempty settings; defaults only at tenant creation; one resolver                       | Resolved: required canonical unique settings fail on empty, invalid, or duplicate values |\n| F-042 | Medium   | Manual-approval email prints a raw UTC ISO deadline                                                                                | Pass tenant timezone and format a clear `de-DE` local deadline with zone                         | Resolved: the timezone is required and invalid persisted zones fail before enqueue       |\n| F-043 | Medium   | Email-outbox overview can displace old unresolved incidents with newer routine rows                                                | Cursor/status filtering or unresolved-first ordering                                             | Resolved                                                                                 |\n\n### Database and domain integrity\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                               | Required simple outcome                                                       | Status                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ----- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| F-044 | High     | Template/event discounts lacked keys, owner FKs, uniqueness, and nonnegative checks                                                | Composite owner FKs, unique type per option, keys, and nonnegative checks     | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| F-045 | High     | Registration question/answer ownership, receipt/event/refund ownership, and payment provenance still rely partly on service checks | Composite tenant/owner foreign keys and focused invalid-row tests             | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| F-046 | Medium   | Quantities, counters, receipt sizes/amounts/status relationships, and lifecycle timestamps lack DB checks                          | Add direct constraints for domain ranges/state relationships                  | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| F-047 | Medium   | Persisted tenant/receipt/discount decoding sometimes supplies plausible defaults                                                   | Make persisted decoding strict; creation code owns defaults                   | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| F-048 | Medium   | Communication email and payout identifiers are weakly validated                                                                    | Nonempty canonical email, PayPal email schema, normalized checksum-valid IBAN | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| F-049 | Medium   | Candidate indexes are inferred rather than measured                                                                                | Confirm with representative `EXPLAIN`; add only proven indexes                | Accepted: D-003 measurement exposed the repeated option-existence path, so only the direct `event_registration_options(eventId)` B-tree was added; the 36-row seed still chose a 0.130 ms hash/sequence plan, and no speculative composite or GIN index was added |\n\n### Administration and user experience\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                                  | Required simple outcome                                                    | Status                                                              |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| F-050 | High     | Admin overview fires review/role queries without the required permissions and then hides 403s                                         | Gate queries by capability and render real failure states                  | Resolved                                                            |\n| F-051 | High     | Regular tenant Stripe tax-rate administration silently succeeds with no account, reads only 100, and imports unbounded/inactive rates | One bounded tenant tax-rate service shared with the stricter platform path | Resolved                                                            |\n| F-052 | Medium   | General settings truncate fractional limits and silently clamp invalid values                                                         | Integer/nonnegative schemas and inline errors; no coercion                 | Resolved                                                            |\n| F-053 | Medium   | Role create/edit failures are invisible; regular/platform validation diverges                                                         | One role-write normalizer and visible typed duplicate/validation errors    | Resolved                                                            |\n| F-054 | Medium   | Icon-only controls lack accessible names and required role fields do not render their errors                                          | Accessible labels and inline validation at the field                       | Resolved                                                            |\n| F-055 | Medium   | Platform finance/admin mutations use generic catch messages instead of typed outcomes                                                 | Use the shared typed error renderer                                        | Resolved: finance and non-finance mutations use the shared renderer |\n\n### Operations, tests, and release behavior\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                                                                                   | Required simple outcome                                                                                                                                                                            | Status                                                                                      |\n| ----- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| F-056 | High     | Local `db:push` can target an exported remote `DATABASE_URL`                                                                                                                           | Refuse anything except the explicit local/loopback database boundary                                                                                                                               | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-057 | High     | Staging RPC smoke considered a raw `Defect` response success                                                                                                                           | Assert a meaningful typed success/auth-boundary outcome                                                                                                                                            | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-058 | High     | Partial seed failures could still write initialized state; paid fixtures and declared seed records still accepted missing prerequisites                                                | Atomic truthful marker, exact paid-fixture prerequisites, required declared records, and no arbitrary fallbacks                                                                                    | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-059 | High     | Reused images can skip equivalent security checks and Trivy ignores unfixed findings                                                                                                   | Scan every exact digest and use explicit reviewed waivers only                                                                                                                                     | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-060 | Medium   | Release gates can select an older successful run rather than the latest completed exact SHA                                                                                            | Gate on the exact intended revision/run                                                                                                                                                            | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-061 | Medium   | Playwright fixture swallows malformed runtime state, globally ignores HTTPS errors, and hides tenant-cookie setup failure                                                              | Only ENOENT means absent; explicit local-only TLS exception; fail setup visibly                                                                                                                    | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-062 | Medium   | `.dockerignore` sends test/auth/report/vendor material; Docker apt upgrade is nondeterministic                                                                                         | Minimize build context and pin deterministic base/package behavior                                                                                                                                 | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-063 | Medium   | Invalid explicit `APP_HOST_PORT` falls back; robots/sitemap hardcode the alpha host; private ops curl lacks timeouts                                                                   | Reject invalid config, derive canonical host, and use bounded calls                                                                                                                                | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-064 | Medium   | Worker readiness was previously absent                                                                                                                                                 | Recheck the new worker email readiness route against deployment probes before closing                                                                                                              | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-093 | High     | The exact production runtime image scan reported four Critical and 21 High Debian package findings, including four Critical `perl-base` CVEs                                           | Use a pinned minimal runtime containing only Bun and required application artifacts; no waiver, suppression, broad package upgrade, shell wrapper, or scanner fallback                             | Resolved                                                                                    |\n| F-094 | Medium   | The real credential-backed Playwright baseline exposed 30 stale fresh-schema constraint fixtures, outdated assertions, and mutable shared-identity failures after 120/150 tests passed | Align fixtures with current review, price-snapshot, and confirmed-state invariants; update stale assertions; isolate mutable test identities; require green functional and documentation baselines | Resolved: real Auth0 functional 153/153 and provider-backed documentation publication 54/54 |\n\n### Removed compatibility and stale artifacts\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                           | Required simple outcome                                                                  | Status   |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| F-065 | High     | `migration/**`, `old/**`, `drizzle.config.old.ts`, migration-only tests/config, and `db:migrate` implemented a legacy importer | Delete the complete path and now-unused dependencies/config exceptions                   | Resolved |\n| F-066 | Medium   | Stored `random` registration mode and writable/readable compatibility branches survived the relaunch contract                  | Remove the mode from DB, contracts, UI, services, platform tools, docs, and tests        | Resolved |\n| F-067 | Medium   | Persisted tenant locale duplicated the fixed `de-DE` product invariant                                                         | Remove the column/type/context and use the invariant directly                            | Resolved |\n| F-068 | Medium   | `admin:manageTaxes` aliased `admin:tax`; `collapseMembersInHup` had no implemented behavior                                    | Remove both end to end                                                                   | Resolved |\n| F-069 | Medium   | Obsolete simple-template RPC/service and a second unused template-form cluster duplicated the graph path                       | Delete them and keep the canonical graph flow                                            | Resolved |\n| F-070 | Low      | Historical compliance ledger and deployment-data audit scripts described old releases/data repair                              | Replace with this queue and delete the scripts                                           | Resolved |\n| F-073 | Medium   | A broad `roles: all` legacy E2E account made unrelated profile/template tests pass with excessive authority                    | Scope the profile account as a regular user and use explicit admin state for admin tests | Resolved |\n\n### Settled-decision implementation follow-up\n\n| ID    | Severity | Finding and evidence                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | Required simple outcome                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Status                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| F-096 | High     | Tenant and platform settings accepted an arbitrary non-empty Stripe account ID on initial connection, deferring the defect until a later paid flow                                                                                                                                   | Remove account attachment from client settings; validate the exact account in one private first-attachment operation before persistence, while keeping provider or contract failures visible                                                                               | Resolved: client write fields are deleted, and the private attach-once operation validates the account before taking the tenant lock and writing                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| F-097 | High     | Direct and manual-approval registration Checkout builders could serialize a positive-priced included-only add-on as a zero-quantity Stripe line                                                                                                                                      | Add a Checkout line only when both unit price and purchased quantity are positive; keep the included entitlement unchanged                                                                                                                                                 | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-098 | Medium   | The focused-settings documentation title generated a new slug while publication still required the deleted monolithic-settings slug                                                                                                                                                  | Update the exact publication source contract and keep its fail-closed bundle test green                                                                                                                                                                                    | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-099 | Medium   | Event permissions and generated guidance encode configurable four-way audiences for ordinary optionful events, while the current product direction derives their discovery directly from registration-option eligibility                                                             | Remove ordinary audience controls and guidance; document option-derived ordinary discovery and selected-role announcement visibility as intentionally different rules that grant no access or notifications                                                                | Resolved: ordinary audience permissions, RPCs, UI, and guides are deleted; announcement discovery is named and documented as its own visibility-only operation                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| F-100 | Medium   | The first routed profile shell constructed the overview before a direct child route activated, so child pages still started the overview's personal-data query                                                                                                                       | Make overview the explicit default child route and let each routed page exclusively own its data                                                                                                                                                                           | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-101 | Medium   | Profile add-on summaries used Angular's default currency and multiplied the paid unit price by total entitlement, including free included units                                                                                                                                      | Carry the tenant currency and purchased quantity in the typed summary; display only the amount paid for purchased units                                                                                                                                                    | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-102 | High     | A payment-settings form opened on Stripe account A could overwrite a concurrent change to B because request-start reads did not carry the form's original account                                                                                                                    | Delete account mutation from tenant and platform settings; under the only remaining attach path, lock the tenant and require the account to remain unset before writing                                                                                                    | Resolved: the settings mutation fields and stale-account overwrite path are deleted; the attach-once operation rejects an already configured tenant under lock                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| F-103 | Medium   | Stripe account and tax-rate validation converted broad invalid-request, network, authentication, rate-limit, malformed-response, and mismatched-ID failures into ordinary unavailable input                                                                                          | Map only Stripe's definitive 404 `resource_missing` response to unavailable input; preserve every other provider or contract failure as a defect                                                                                                                           | Resolved: account and tax-rate lookups now classify only the exact missing-resource response as recoverable, and focused negative tests keep every other invalid request in the defect channel                                                                                                                                 |\n| F-104 | Medium   | Tenant-admin optionless-announcement visibility failures were silent, and Save could close before the role catalog proved every selected discovery role still existed                                                                                                                | Fail closed until the role catalog is valid and show the exact mutation failure; an empty validated selection remains link-only                                                                                                                                            | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-105 | Medium   | Focused settings pages discarded dirty edits on sibling navigation and unconditionally overwrote them when tenant configuration refreshed                                                                                                                                            | Guard all five routes, hydrate only pristine forms, reset after successful saves, and require initialized tenant state                                                                                                                                                     | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-106 | Medium   | Appearance settings could save old asset URLs while a file upload was still running and then leave the uploaded URL as unmarked unsaved state                                                                                                                                        | Disable and guard Save through file read/upload; mark the returned local URL dirty until the focused settings save succeeds                                                                                                                                                | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-107 | Medium   | Individually valid registration, guest, and add-on prices could overflow PostgreSQL integer aggregates and surface an internal SQL failure after entering checkout                                                                                                                   | Bound each lot, subtotal, and combined total with `BigInt` before reservation or persistence and return a typed conflict                                                                                                                                                   | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-108 | Medium   | Mobile profile navigation removed the focused link without moving focus, while detail pages duplicated the shell heading and retained fragment-era layout residue                                                                                                                    | Focus the routed detail heading, keep one page-level heading, preserve mobile spacing, and delete the obsolete receipt fragment                                                                                                                                            | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-109 | Medium   | Stripe-backed Playwright tried to execute `cat` inside the intentionally shell-less distroless application image, so signed webhook tests could not read the mounted listener secret                                                                                                 | Read the file through the shipped Bun runtime; keep the running container authoritative and retain the fail-closed timeout                                                                                                                                                 | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-110 | Low      | The advanced-template snapshot journey and persistence model preserve a copied template discovery default even though templates now define structure only and have no visibility or default audience                                                                                 | Delete the template audience field and copied-default assertion; verify the structural snapshot separately and prove event discovery from the created event's options                                                                                                      | Resolved: template state and forms are structural only; the snapshot journey proves structure while event discovery is verified independently from copied options                                                                                                                                                              |\n| F-111 | Medium   | Server-rendered focused settings forms left native controls active before Angular hydration and event replay; an early submit performed a native GET before replayed `preventDefault` threw                                                                                          | Keep the complete form disabled through browser render and application stability, then enable it; guard every save with the same readiness signal                                                                                                                          | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-112 | Low      | The legal-settings Playwright readback selected the derived `privacyPolicyUrl` projection as if it were a tenant column, so Drizzle rejected the nested selection before checking the save                                                                                           | Assert only the legal-notice and terms columns owned by this focused settings page; do not add a compatibility field                                                                                                                                                       | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-113 | Low      | The event-discovery guide selected the first page-wide `Events` link, so the new profile-section link shadowed the documented main-navigation destination                                                                                                                            | Scope the journey to the explicitly labelled main navigation; keep the distinct public-event and profile-event destinations visible                                                                                                                                        | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-114 | Low      | Two touched seed helpers used avoidable `../src` paths for database and shared modules even though their existing runtime supports the repository aliases                                                                                                                            | Use the existing `@db` and `@shared` aliases locally; keep the direct tenant-type import and do not add lint machinery or sweep unrelated helpers                                                                                                                          | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-115 | Low      | The documented `@types/*` application alias occupies TypeScript's declaration-package namespace; Angular rejected it with TS6137 and Playwright could not resolve it                                                                                                                 | Delete the invalid alias, update its three test consumers and repository guidance, and keep application-type imports direct                                                                                                                                                | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-116 | Medium   | The Docker/Playwright preflight accepted a short session secret that the application rejected during startup, so a nominally valid test environment failed later with a different contract                                                                                           | Enforce the application's minimum 32-byte UTF-8 secret at preflight and keep the shared development value valid; do not add an application fallback                                                                                                                        | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-117 | Medium   | Identity-aware event query keys left the capacity and registration card stale after cancellation because exact invalidation targeted only the old unsuffixed key                                                                                                                     | Invalidate the event-details key prefix and prove active observers refresh; do not maintain parallel identity-specific invalidation lists                                                                                                                                  | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-118 | High     | Paid-transfer finalization locked event state before recipient membership while normal registration locked membership before event state, allowing a real PostgreSQL deadlock cycle                                                                                                  | Reuse the canonical membership → roles → option/event lock order and prove the competing flows serialize to one registration plus an explicit conflict                                                                                                                     | Resolved                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| F-119 | High     | Application errors, announcement controls, email status, and generated guides exposed implementation names, raw service diagnostics, internal identifiers, and test evidence to users                                                                                                | Replace them with plain task, outcome, and next-action language; keep unexpected failures visible and retain technical diagnostics only in logs and executable assertions                                                                                                  | Resolved: application, email, public errors, and generated-guide inventories use task/outcome/next-action language; source and generated-output guards reject the removed implementation wording                                                                                                                               |\n| F-120 | High     | Client tenant configuration and tenant/platform administration exposed and accepted the raw connected payment-account identifier, letting ordinary screens attach, rotate, or disconnect the account                                                                                 | Expose readiness only; keep the identifier server-side; permit one private, explicitly confirmed first attachment for that organization with validation, locking, fresh-tenant guards, and a status-only audit; support no rotation or disconnect                          | Resolved: client projections and writes expose readiness only; one private attach validates the account and expected organization under lock, refuses non-fresh state, and has no rotation or disconnect path                                                                                                                  |\n| F-121 | High     | The private Scaleway invocation helper accepted an arbitrary HTTPS URL and placed both cloud credentials and the payment-account body in process arguments, allowing credential disclosure or exfiltration                                                                           | Resolve one exact role endpoint from reviewed Terraform output, bind role/path pairs, bypass proxies and redirects, and pass secrets/body without exposing them in arguments or child environment                                                                          | Resolved: the helper rejects unreviewed projects, hosts, paths, roles, redirects, and proxy use before invocation; deterministic tests prove the secret and body are absent from curl arguments and environment                                                                                                                |\n| F-122 | High     | Platform change-history responses could carry raw payment-account IDs in nested snapshots or free-form reasons; initial redaction also made same-count tax-rate updates look corrupt                                                                                                 | Keep persisted evidence internal, project explicit safe scalar summaries, reject payment-account tokens in every operator reason, and render normal tax-rate update/add/unchanged outcomes                                                                                 | Resolved: RPC output contains safe fields/counts only, tax-rate batches expose understandable added/updated/up-to-date counts, and all platform reasons are trimmed and reject `acct_…` tokens                                                                                                                                 |\n| F-123 | High     | The irreversible first payment attachment trusted only opaque organization/account IDs, accepted weak audit reasons, and lacked real PostgreSQL proof that concurrent first attachments serialize                                                                                    | Require and lock-check the expected organization domain, trim and validate a non-identifying reason, and prove two concurrent attempts to one organization yield one audited winner and one explicit refusal                                                               | Resolved: domain mismatch, blank/identifier-bearing reasons, concurrent first attachments, and pending work have focused unit/route/PostgreSQL coverage                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| F-124 | Medium   | Removed payment-account fields on the ordinary admin settings RPC were silently stripped, so a stale client could receive success while believing an unsupported account change occurred                                                                                             | Reject every excess legacy field at the transport boundary; do not strip or emulate deleted account writes                                                                                                                                                                 | Resolved: ordinary and platform tenant update contracts fail on removed outer or nested account fields, with no compatibility branch                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| F-125 | High     | One payment account may be attached to multiple Evorto organizations; this is now an intentional shared-account model                                                                                                                                                                | Document the shared-account boundary, preserve organization isolation, and add no cross-organization uniqueness rule or compatibility path                                                                                                                                 | Accepted: D-008 permits account reuse. Sharing payment processing does not share members, events, settings, authority, or payment records.                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| F-126 | High     | The documented lint gate silently excluded `tests/**/*.ts`, hiding 61 findings across 18 test files and allowing test code to drift outside the repository's TypeScript rules                                                                                                        | Include Playwright, documentation, and support tests in the Node-side lint scope; fix the findings without blanket suppressions; preserve Playwright's required empty fixture-object callback shape through one narrow rule option                                         | Resolved: tests are now linted, all 61 findings are fixed, and the callback contract is preserved by the scoped `no-empty-pattern` option                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| F-127 | Medium   | Saving who can find an announcement closed the dialog and refreshed data without confirming success, leaving the organizer to infer whether the change was kept                                                                                                                      | Confirm the completed save in both the tenant-admin and platform-admin announcement controls; keep failures explicit and covered separately                                                                                                                                | Resolved: both announcement controls now confirm that who can find the announcement was updated, with focused component and generated-guide coverage                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| F-128 | Medium   | The final whole-product copy audit found technical nouns, internal identifiers, stale sign-up/refund terminology, weak screenshot captions, storage-oriented “record” phrases, and generated pages whose heading/frontmatter ownership could drift after the earlier focused cleanup | Complete the application, email, public-error, and generated-guide inventory; enforce plain task/outcome/next-action wording plus one valid generated page structure; keep diagnostics only in logs and executable assertions                                              | Resolved: application, email, public/server copy, and all 13 published guides use plain product language; source and final-output guards reject the identified wording and malformed guide structure, including ATX, Setext, and raw HTML level-one headings; the provider-backed publication passes 54/54                     |\n| F-129 | Medium   | The ticket page could decide whether a payment page for add-ons had expired from its timestamp and the device clock, allowing the visible state to disagree with server truth                                                                                                        | Compute the state once on the server, project one explicit boolean, and leave the timestamp display-only; add no retry or fallback path                                                                                                                                    | Resolved: the server projects `pendingCheckoutExpired`; contracts and server/component/Playwright coverage prove active and expired states, and the client no longer guesses expiry                                                                                                                                            |\n| F-130 | Medium   | Local Compose published the web app, PostgreSQL, Mailpit, and MinIO beyond the loopback interface; stale Docker Desktop forwards also let the wrong local instance answer selected ports and produced misleading authentication/test failures                                        | Bind every developer-facing port to loopback, clear only the stale forwarding state, restore the exact review stack without resetting unrelated data, and verify the selected instance through full browser coverage                                                       | Resolved: Compose and its source contract require `127.0.0.1`; Docker forwarding was cleared, the review stack is healthy on port 4200, the unrelated stack retained its intended state, and 153/153 functional plus 54/54 provider-backed documentation journeys pass                                                         |\n| F-131 | Medium   | The runtime environment port-allocation test sampled 10,001 seeds and made roughly 100,000 assertions, causing a false five-second timeout under the full server suite even though disjoint port ranges structurally guarantee the invariant                                         | Keep representative and boundary regression seeds only: `288`, `worktree-0`, and `worktree-9999`; do not brute-force a structurally guaranteed range                                                                                                                       | Resolved: the reduced boundary suite covers all seven runtime-port assertions in 4 ms                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| F-132 | High     | The app documentation publisher still validated a removed Pages layout, while the app bundle catalog, Pages catalog, navigation, and generated guide slugs had drifted apart; the supported publication command could not update the real consumer                                   | Validate the two tracked marketing destinations, keep one exact 13-guide catalog on both sides, and let only the official all-project publication replace generated output; do not copy a baseline-only or stale bundle                                                    | Resolved: the official all-project run passed 54/54 and transactionally published the exact 13-guide catalog to both tracked Pages destinations; no stale or partial publication path remains                                                                                                                                  |\n| F-133 | Medium   | Generated screenshots could capture event, check-in, role, change-history, tax-rate, and template pages while their content was still loading, even though their captions described completed states                                                                                 | Require the exact completed content or enabled action before each capture, and fail every capture that still contains visible loading copy                                                                                                                                 | Resolved: the full run exposed and directly repaired one remaining role-page hydration barrier; exact completion checks plus the global fail-loud guard then produced a clean 54/54 provider-backed publication without retry or timeout changes                                                                               |\n| F-134 | Medium   | Generated screenshots exposed test/internal wording through `TEST-ESN-0001` and “settled fulfillment history” fixture text                                                                                                                                                           | Use realistic public examples and ordinary event wording; keep test identity and fulfillment mechanics out of product documentation                                                                                                                                        | Resolved: the visible identifier and add-on descriptions are plain product examples, guarded at source, and absent from the final generated output                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| F-135 | Medium   | Public helper-supplied server messages bypassed the RPC error-copy guard and told users to select “Refresh” or choose a “browser tab icon”                                                                                                                                           | Use the actual action and product object names, and include `failureMessage` and `publicMessage` properties in the server plain-language guard                                                                                                                             | Resolved: the copy now says “Check again” and “small site icon”; the expanded eight-test server copy guard passes                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| F-136 | Medium   | The Pages site retained a backwards-compatible transfer-receive page with obsolete product claims and three homepage references to missing generated screenshots                                                                                                                     | Delete the compatibility page and broken image coupling; keep one current transfer guide and a text-first homepage until real durable assets exist                                                                                                                         | Resolved in [Pages PR #15](https://github.com/heddendorp/evorto/pull/15): current destinations are populated, the obsolete route and broken image coupling are absent, and 19/19 tooling 