{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T07:17:14.131Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019fd5ee-f112-7ea0-9928-9e5a0d318640","author":"/root/pr_submission_manifest","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr_submission_manifest\nPayload:\nRead-only live manifest captured on 2026-08-06:\n\n- Trunk: `main` at `d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea`\n- Current/top branch: `codex/staging-latency-runbooks`\n- Layers: 99\n- `needsRebase`: false for all layers\n- Only overlapping remote branches are the old heads for #123 and #124.\n- Only existing PRs among all 99 branch names are:\n  - #123 at position 95, open and ready, remote head `951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f`\n  - #124 at position 99, open and ready, remote head `d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9`\n- No refs, files, PRs, remotes, Docker state, or worktree content were changed.\n\n## Layer manifest\n\n```text\nPos Branch                                                      PR   Subject\n01  codex/remove-prior-compliance-artifacts                     -    chore: remove prior compliance artifacts\n02  codex/remove-dead-runtime-dependencies                      -    refactor: remove dead runtime dependencies\n03  codex/remove-legacy-migration-tools                         -    refactor: remove legacy migration runner\n04  codex/remove-tenant-migration-steps                         -    refactor: remove tenant migration steps\n05  codex/remove-identity-migration-steps                       -    refactor: remove identity migration steps\n06  codex/remove-event-migration-steps                          -    refactor: remove event migration steps\n07  codex/remove-legacy-event-mapping-rules                     -    refactor: remove legacy event mapping rules\n08  codex/remove-migration-support-utilities                    -    refactor: remove migration support utilities\n09  codex/remove-migration-repository-wiring                    -    refactor: remove migration repository wiring\n10  codex/remove-legacy-schema-module                           -    refactor: remove legacy schema module\n11  codex/remove-legacy-schema-history                          -    refactor: remove legacy schema history\n12  codex/remove-generated-legacy-snapshot                      -    refactor: remove generated legacy snapshot\n13  codex/remove-invalid-types-alias                            -    refactor: remove invalid types alias\n14  codex/guard-local-drizzle-targets                           -    fix: keep local database commands on one target\n15  codex/require-explicit-seed-context                         -    fix: require explicit atomic seed context\n16  codex/fail-closed-local-seeding                             -    fix: fail closed local database reset\n17  codex/reuse-primary-provider-credentials                    -    test: reuse primary provider credentials\n18  codex/harden-brand-asset-storage                            -    fix: harden tenant brand asset storage\n19  codex/use-production-shaped-tenant-fixtures                 -    test: use production-shaped tenant fixtures\n20  codex/fail-closed-local-runtime-state                       -    test: make local runtime state fail closed\n21  codex/harden-container-runtime-image                        -    build: harden container runtime image\n22  codex/enforce-registration-graph-integrity                  -    fix: enforce registration graph integrity\n23  codex/settle-registration-addons-in-one-checkout            -    feat: settle registration add-ons in one checkout\n24  codex/define-registration-transfer-claim-rules              -    feat: define registration transfer claim rules\n25  codex/harden-transfer-refund-recovery                       -    fix: harden transfer refund recovery\n26  codex/guard-transfer-acquisition-data                       -    fix: guard transfer acquisition data\n27  codex/remove-direct-registration-reassignment               -    refactor: remove direct registration reassignment\n28  codex/use-private-registration-transfer-claims              -    feat: use private transfer claim codes\n29  codex/add-private-transfer-claim-interface                  -    feat: expose private registration transfer claims\n30  codex/attach-organization-payment-account                   -    feat: attach first organization payment account\n31  codex/prove-payment-account-attachment-serialization        -    test: verify payment account attachment serialization\n32  codex/add-private-payment-account-setup-route               -    feat: expose private payment account setup\n33  codex/refresh-default-application-theme                     -    feat: refresh default application theme\n34  codex/report-client-failures-safely                         -    fix: report client failures safely\n35  codex/simplify-shared-form-controls                         -    refactor: simplify shared form controls\n36  codex/clarify-application-access-boundaries                 -    fix: clarify application access boundaries\n37  codex/serialize-and-bound-ticket-check-in                   -    fix: serialize and bound ticket check-in\n38  codex/make-scanner-recovery-explicit                        -    fix: make scanner recovery explicit\n39  codex/use-plain-scanner-and-addon-language                  -    refactor: use plain scanner and add-on language\n40  codex/harden-ticket-qr-responses                            -    fix: harden ticket QR responses\n41  codex/validate-tenant-website-addresses                     -    fix: validate tenant website addresses\n42  codex/explain-blocked-tenant-integrity-changes              -    fix: explain blocked tenant integrity changes\n43  codex/normalize-tenant-role-authority                       -    refactor: normalize tenant role authority\n44  codex/harden-auth-identity-boundaries                       -    fix: harden auth identity boundaries\n45  codex/refresh-onboarding-identity-state                     -    fix: refresh onboarding identity state\n46  codex/prepare-isolated-hosting-state-roots                  -    infra: prepare isolated Scaleway state roots\n47  codex/cut-over-hosting-environment-state                    -    infra: cut over Scaleway environment state\n48  codex/fail-closed-release-gates                             -    ci: make Scaleway release gates fail closed\n49  codex/make-hosting-deployments-forward-only                 -    fix: make Scaleway deployments forward-only\n50  codex/align-local-secrets-with-hardened-runtime             -    fix: align local secrets with hardened runtime\n51  codex/require-explicit-organization-configuration           -    refactor: require explicit tenant configuration\n52  codex/expose-focused-organization-settings-mutations       -    refactor: expose focused tenant settings mutations\n53  codex/project-client-safe-organization-configuration        -    refactor: project client-safe tenant configuration\n54  codex/add-organization-registration-settings                -    feat: add organization and registration settings\n55  codex/add-appearance-payment-and-legal-settings             -    feat: add appearance payment and legal settings\n56  codex/route-focused-organization-settings-pages             -    refactor: route focused tenant settings pages\n57  codex/prove-organization-configuration-boundaries           -    test: prove tenant configuration boundaries\n58  codex/harden-role-and-member-administration                 -    refactor: harden role and member administration\n59  codex/remove-obsolete-user-attributes                       -    refactor: remove obsolete user attributes\n60  codex/validate-profile-identity-fields                      -    fix: validate profile identity fields\n61  codex/recheck-registration-eligibility-on-writes            -    fix: recheck registration eligibility at every write\n62  codex/refund-paid-signups-after-access-changes              -    fix: refund paid signups when access changes\n63  codex/use-complete-template-authoring                       -    refactor: use complete template authoring\n64  codex/remove-obsolete-simple-template-coverage              -    test: remove obsolete simple template coverage\n65  codex/remove-obsolete-template-api                          -    refactor: remove obsolete template api\n66  codex/delete-retired-template-form-helpers                  -    refactor: delete retired template form helpers\n67  codex/harden-receipt-evidence-storage                       -    fix: harden receipt evidence storage\n68  codex/validate-finance-receipt-contracts                    -    fix: validate finance receipt contracts\n69  codex/enforce-finance-receipt-mutations                     -    fix: enforce finance receipt mutations\n70  codex/simplify-receipt-reimbursements                       -    refactor: simplify receipt reimbursements\n71  codex/improve-receipt-submission-finance-views              -    feat: improve receipt submission and finance views\n72  codex/make-email-delivery-single-dispatch                   -    fix: make email delivery single dispatch\n73  codex/simplify-email-outbox-records-overview                -    refactor: simplify email outbox records and overview\n74  codex/focus-profile-account-overview                        -    refactor: focus profile account overview\n75  codex/separate-profile-discounts                            -    refactor: separate profile discounts\n76  codex/route-focused-profile-pages                           -    refactor: route focused profile pages\n77  codex/define-event-discovery-rules                          -    docs: define event discovery rules\n78  codex/make-templates-structure-only                         -    refactor: make templates structure only\n79  codex/derive-event-discovery-from-sign-up-options           -    refactor: derive event discovery from sign-up options\n80  codex/target-information-only-events-by-role                -    feat: target information-only events by role\n81  codex/harden-platform-administration-contracts              -    fix: harden platform administration contracts\n82  codex/prove-organization-administration-and-member-access   -    test: prove organization administration and member access\n83  codex/explain-organization-and-platform-administration      -    docs: explain organization and platform administration\n84  codex/prove-profile-discounts-and-onboarding-journeys       -    test: prove profile, discounts, and onboarding journeys\n85  codex/prove-event-discovery-approval-and-templates          -    test: prove event discovery, approval, and templates\n86  codex/explain-event-discovery-and-publishing                -    docs: explain event discovery and publishing\n87  codex/prove-registration-and-ticket-lifecycle               -    test: prove registration and ticket lifecycle\n88  codex/prove-scanning-and-fulfillment-journeys               -    test: prove scanning and fulfillment journeys\n89  codex/prove-finance-receipts-and-webhook-recovery           -    test: prove finance, receipts, and webhook recovery\n90  codex/publish-plain-language-generated-guides               -    test: publish plain-language generated guides\n91  codex/guard-generated-guide-sources                         -    test: guard generated guide sources\n92  codex/use-plain-application-language                        -    refactor: use plain application language\n93  codex/make-acceptance-failures-explicit                     -    test: make acceptance failures explicit\n94  codex/bound-local-docker-lifecycle                          -    fix: bound local Docker lifecycle commands\n95  codex/full-application-simplification-review                123  docs: record application review checkpoint\n96  codex/trace-staging-request-latency                         -    perf: trace staging request latency\n97  codex/add-bounded-staging-latency-probe                     -    feat: add bounded staging latency probe\n98  codex/automate-staging-latency-evidence                     -    ci: automate staging latency evidence\n99  codex/staging-latency-runbooks                              124  docs: explain staging latency response\n```\n\n## Replacement text for #123\n\nTitle:\n\n```text\ndocs: record application review checkpoint\n```\n\nBody:\n\n```markdown\n## Purpose\n\nPersist the application-wide manual review checkpoint so findings, simplification decisions, and remaining proof are reviewable in the repository rather than held in chat history.\n\n## This layer\n\n- Adds `APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md` only: 1 file, 1,305 added lines.\n- Records all 157 finding outcomes, including 155 resolved findings and 2 explicitly accepted boundaries.\n- Preserves all 41 simplification candidates and product decisions D-001 through D-008.\n- Separates the reconstructed source-review checkpoint from historical evidence and the final-stack evidence that still has to be recorded.\n- Adds no application code.\n\n## Stack context\n\nThis is layer 95 of 99. It depends on the preceding 94 implementation layers; the four staging-latency layers follow it.\n\n## Verification status\n\nThis PR does not claim completion of the 99-head or integrated environment gates. Those requirements remain explicit in the review queue until their actual final-stack evidence is recorded.\n```\n\n## Replacement text for #124\n\nTitle:\n\n```text\ndocs: add staging latency improvement and monitoring runbooks\n```\n\nBody:\n\n```markdown\n## Purpose\n\nTurn the dated staging-latency evidence into an explicit improvement and incident-response playbook.\n\n## This layer\n\n- Adds `LATENCY_IMPROVEMENT.md` with the dated baseline, provisional budgets, ordered improvement plan, and evidence record.\n- Adds `infrastructure/scaleway/LATENCY_MONITORING.md` with warm-candidate sampling, trace and dashboard guidance, report-only thresholds, and incident response.\n- Links those runbooks from `QUALITY.md` and the Scaleway README.\n- Adds one documentation contract proving that the planned `config.bootstrap` trace signal is not presented as active.\n- Changes 5 files with 608 added lines and no runtime behavior.\n\n## Stack context\n\nThis is layer 99 of 99. It documents how to operate and continue the tracing, bounded probe, and CI evidence introduced in layers 96–98. It does not implement the planned bootstrap endpoint or activate its metric.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nNo current performance claim is made here. The recorded baseline is explicitly dated 2026-07-27, and the proposed latency thresholds remain provisional or report-only until accepted evidence activates them.\n```\n\n## Exact submission sequence\n\nRun only after every required local branch-head and integrated gate is green.\n\n### 1. Shape and lease checks\n\n```zsh\nset -euo pipefail\ncd /Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto\n\ngit diff --quiet --ignore-submodules --\ngit diff --cached --quiet --ignore-submodules --\ntest -z \"$(git ls-files --others --exclude-standard)\"\ntest \"$(git branch --show-current)\" = \"codex/staging-latency-runbooks\"\n\ngit fetch --no-tags origin \\\n  '+refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main' \\\n  '+refs/heads/codex/full-application-simplification-review:refs/remotes/origin/codex/full-application-simplification-review' \\\n  '+refs/heads/codex/staging-latency-runbooks:refs/remotes/origin/codex/staging-latency-runbooks'\n\ntest \"$(git rev-parse main)\" = \"d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea\"\ntest \"$(git rev-parse refs/remotes/origin/main)\" = \"d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea\"\ntest \"$(git rev-parse refs/remotes/origin/codex/full-application-simplification-review)\" = \"951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f\"\ntest \"$(git rev-parse refs/remotes/origin/codex/staging-latency-runbooks)\" = \"d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9\"\n\ngh stack view --json | jq -e '\n  .trunk == \"main\"\n  and .currentBranch == \"codex/staging-latency-runbooks\"\n  and ((.branches | length) == 99)\n  and all(.branches[]; (.needsRebase | not) and (.isMerged | not) and (.isQueued | not))\n  and .branches[94].name == \"codex/full-application-simplification-review\"\n  and .branches[98].name == \"codex/staging-latency-runbooks\"\n  and ([.branches[] | select(.pr != null) | .pr.number] == [123, 124])\n' >/dev/null\n\nevorto_stack_parent=main\nwhile IFS= read -r evorto_stack_branch; do\n  git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$evorto_stack_parent\" \"$evorto_stack_branch\"\n  test \"$(git rev-list --count \"${evorto_stack_parent}..${evorto_stack_branch}\")\" -eq 1\n  evorto_layer_files=\"$(\n    git diff --name-only \"${evorto_stack_parent}..${evorto_stack_branch}\" -- |\n      awk 'NF { count++ } END { print count + 0 }'\n  )\"\n  test \"$evorto_layer_files\" -gt 0\n  test \"$evorto_layer_files\" -lt 100\n  evorto_stack_parent=\"$evorto_stack_branch\"\ndone < <(gh stack view --json | jq -r '.branches[].name')\n\nevorto_stack_remote_overlap=\"$(\n  comm -12 \\\n    <(gh stack view --json | jq -r '.branches[].name' | LC_ALL=C sort) \\\n    <(git ls-remote --heads origin 'refs/heads/*' |\n        awk '{ sub(\"^refs/heads/\", \"\", $2); print $2 }' |\n        LC_ALL=C sort)\n)\"\ntest \"$evorto_stack_remote_overlap\" = $'codex/full-application-simplification-review\\ncodex/staging-latency-runbooks'\n\ntest \"$(\n  git ls-remote --heads origin refs/heads/codex/full-application-simplification-review |\n    awk '{ print $1 }'\n)\" = \"951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f\"\n\ntest \"$(\n  git ls-remote --heads origin refs/heads/codex/staging-latency-runbooks |\n    awk '{ print $1 }'\n)\" = \"d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9\"\n\njq -e -s '\n  . as $docs\n  | ($docs[0].branches | map(.name)) as $names\n  | ($docs[1] | map(select(.headRefName as $head | $names | index($head)))) as $prs\n  | (($prs | length) == 2)\n    and (($prs | map(.number) | sort) == [123, 124])\n    and all($prs[]; .state == \"OPEN\" and (.isDraft | not))\n    and any($prs[];\n      .number == 123\n      and .headRefName == \"codex/full-application-simplification-review\"\n      and .headRefOid == \"951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f\"\n      and .baseRefName == \"main\"\n    )\n    and any($prs[];\n      .number == 124\n      and .headRefName == \"codex/staging-latency-runbooks\"\n      and .headRefOid == \"d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9\"\n      and .baseRefName == \"main\"\n    )\n' \\\n  <(gh stack view --json) \\\n  <(gh pr list --repo evorto-app/app --state all --limit 1000 \\\n      --json number,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,state,isDraft) \\\n  >/dev/null\n```\n\n### 2. Convert the two existing PRs to drafts\n\n```zsh\ngh pr ready 123 --undo --repo evorto-app/app\ngh pr ready 124 --undo --repo evorto-app/app\n\ngh pr view 123 --repo evorto-app/app \\\n  --json state,isDraft,headRefName,headRefOid |\n  jq -e '\n    .state == \"OPEN\"\n    and .isDraft\n    and .headRefName == \"codex/full-application-simplification-review\"\n    and .headRefOid == \"951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f\"\n  ' >/dev/null\n\ngh pr view 124 --repo evorto-app/app \\\n  --json state,isDraft,headRefName,headRefOid |\n  jq -e '\n    .state == \"OPEN\"\n    and .isDraft\n    and .headRefName == \"codex/staging-latency-runbooks\"\n    and .headRefOid == \"d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9\"\n  ' >/dev/null\n\ntest \"$(\n  git ls-remote --heads origin refs/heads/codex/full-application-simplification-review |\n    awk '{ print $1 }'\n)\" = \"951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f\"\n\ntest \"$(\n  git ls-remote --heads origin refs/heads/codex/staging-latency-runbooks |\n    awk '{ print $1 }'\n)\" = \"d3688389a91075041786fe001aba10e15847abc9\"\n```\n\n### 3. Submit noninteractively\n\n```zsh\ngh stack submit --auto --remote origin\n```\n\n`submit` is not atomic. If a lease rejects a branch, keep the partial remote result visible, re-run the lease checks, resolve only the rejected branch, and rerun the same command.\n\n### 4. Replace #123 and #124 text\n\n```zsh\ngh pr edit 123 --repo evorto-app/app \\\n  --title \"docs: record application review checkpoint\" \\\n  --body-file - <<'EOF'\n## Purpose\n\nPersist the application-wide manual review checkpoint so findings, simplification decisions, and remaining proof are reviewable in the repository rather than held in chat history.\n\n## This layer\n\n- Adds `APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md` only: 1 file, 1,305 added lines.\n- Records all 157 finding outcomes, including 155 resolved findings and 2 explicitly accepted boundaries.\n- Preserves all 41 simplification candidates and product decisions D-001 through D-008.\n- Separates the reconstructed source-review checkpoint from historical evidence and the final-stack evidence that still has to be recorded.\n- Adds no application code.\n\n## Stack context\n\nThis is layer 95 of 99. It depends on the preceding 94 implementation layers; the four staging-latency layers follow it.\n\n## Verification status\n\nThis PR does not claim completion of the 99-head or integrated environment gates. Those requirements remain explicit in the review queue until their actual final-stack evidence is recorded.\nEOF\n\ngh pr edit 124 --repo evorto-app/app \\\n  --title \"docs: add staging latency improvement and monitoring runbooks\" \\\n  --body-file - <<'EOF'\n## Purpose\n\nTurn the dated staging-latency evidence into an explicit improvement and incident-response playbook.\n\n## This layer\n\n- Adds `LATENCY_IMPROVEMENT.md` with the dated baseline, provisional budgets, ordered improvement plan, and evidence record.\n- Adds `infrastructure/scaleway/LATENCY_MONITORING.md` with warm-candidate sampling, trace and dashboard guidance, report-only thresholds, and incident response.\n- Links those runbooks from `QUALITY.md` and the Scaleway README.\n- Adds one documentation contract proving that the planned `config.bootstrap` trace signal is not presented as active.\n- Changes 5 files with 608 added lines and no runtime behavior.\n\n## Stack context\n\nThis is layer 99 of 99. It documents how to operate and continue the tracing, bounded probe, and CI evidence introduced in layers 96–98. It does not implement the planned bootstrap endpoint or activate its metric.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nNo current performance claim is made here. The recorded baseline is explicitly dated 2026-07-27, and the proposed latency thresholds remain provisional or report-only until accepted evidence activates them.\nEOF\n```\n\n### 5. Verify the submitted stack\n\n```zsh\njq -e -s '\n  . as $docs\n  | ($docs[0].branches | map(.name)) as $branches\n  | ($docs[1] | map(select(.headRefName as $head | $branches | index($head)))) as $prs\n  | (($docs[0].branches | length) == 99)\n    and all($docs[0].branches[];\n      ((.pr.number // 0) > 0)\n      and .pr.state == \"OPEN\"\n      and (.needsRebase | not)\n      and (.isMerged | not)\n      and (.isQueued | not)\n    )\n    and (($prs | length) == 99)\n    and all($prs[]; .state == \"OPEN\" and .isDraft)\n    and (\n      [range(0; 99) as $position\n        | ($branches[$position]) as $head\n        | ($prs | map(select(.headRefName == $head))) as $matches\n        | (($matches | length) == 1)\n          and (\n            $matches[0].baseRefName ==\n            (if $position == 0 then \"main\" else $branches[$position - 1] end)\n          )\n      ] | all\n    )\n    and any($prs[];\n      .number == 123\n      and .headRefName == $branches[94]\n      and .headRefOid == \"0fdcf9d080e5d61d4e415e03474ef1bb2980ba9a\"\n      and .baseRefName == $branches[93]\n    )\n    and any($prs[];\n      .number == 124\n      and .headRefName == $branches[98]\n      and .headRefOid == \"e2569f73ba142ec1c395dcf375600a806f798820\"\n      and .baseRefName == $branches[97]\n    )\n' \\\n  <(gh stack view --json) \\\n  <(gh pr list --repo evorto-app/app --state open --limit 1000 \\\n      --json number,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,state,isDraft,title,url) \\\n  >/dev/null\n\ndiff -u \\\n  <(\n    gh stack view --json |\n      jq -r '.branches[].name' |\n      while IFS= read -r evorto_stack_branch; do\n        printf '%s\\t%s\\n' \\\n          \"$evorto_stack_branch\" \\\n          \"$(git rev-parse \"$evorto_stack_branch\")\"\n      done |\n      LC_ALL=C sort\n  ) \\\n  <(\n    gh stack view --json |\n      jq -r '.branches[] | \"refs/heads/\" + .name' |\n      xargs git ls-remote --heads origin |\n      awk '{\n        sub(\"^refs/heads/\", \"\", $2)\n        print $2 \"\\t\" $1\n      }' |\n      LC_ALL=C sort\n  )\n\ngh pr view 123 --repo evorto-app/app \\\n  --json state,isDraft,title,body,baseRefName,headRefOid |\n  jq -e '\n    .state == \"OPEN\"\n    and .isDraft\n    and .title == \"docs: record application review checkpoint\"\n    and .baseRefName == \"codex/bound-local-docker-lifecycle\"\n    and .headRefOid == \"0fdcf9d080e5d61d4e415e03474ef1bb2980ba9a\"\n    and (.body | contains(\"This is layer 95 of 99\"))\n    and (.body | contains(\"does not claim completion\"))\n  ' >/dev/null\n\ngh pr view 124 --repo evorto-app/app \\\n  --json state,isDraft,title,body,baseRefName,headRefOid |\n  jq -e '\n    .state == \"OPEN\"\n    and .isDraft\n    and .title == \"docs: add staging latency improvement and monitoring runbooks\"\n    and .baseRefName == \"codex/automate-staging-latency-evidence\"\n    and .headRefOid == \"e2569f73ba142ec1c395dcf375600a806f798820\"\n    and (.body | contains(\"This is layer 99 of 99\"))\n    and (.body | contains(\"No current performance claim is made\"))\n  ' >/dev/null\n\ngh stack view --json |\n  jq -r '\n    .branches\n    | to_entries[]\n    | \"\\(.key + 1)\\t\\(.value.name)\\t#\\(.value.pr.number)\\t\\(.value.pr.url)\"\n  '\n```"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
