{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T07:48:15.776Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019fd60b-5920-71a1-916c-f40618baab22","call_id":"call_KyZXwpfzDQltQQuB22wBPcs6","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_82_99\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/complete_manifest\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Final 1–99 structural audit: clean; no structural blockers.\\n\\n- Linear stack: 99 first-parent commits, 99 total commits, 99 unique local branch refs, no merges or empty layers.\\n- Largest normal layer by files: position 92, `codex/use-plain-application-language`, 83 files.\\n- Largest normal layer by changed lines: position 85, `codex/prove-event-discovery-approval-and-templates`, +888/-512 = 1,400 lines.\\n- Sole approved exception: `codex/remove-generated-legacy-snapshot`, one file, +0/-3,062.\\n- All subjects and 47 changed changeset versions pass the required wording rules.\\n- Position 95: `0fdcf9d080e5d61d4e415e03474ef1bb2980ba9a`, `codex/full-application-simplification-review`.\\n- Position 99: `e2569f73ba142ec1c395dcf375600a806f798820`, `codex/staging-latency-runbooks`.\\n- Queue integrity matches: 1,305 lines, SHA-256 `f344c0ba2f64a5933ca457a7eca49a769acbe2fd6432798084d89b05d0afc438`; 157 findings, 41 simplification candidates, 8 decisions, and 15 reconstructed coverage rows.\\n- PR124 layers exactly match the isolated replay on every changed blob: 7 files/+195/-105; 2/+764/-0; 3/+112/-1; 5/+608/-0. Sixteen unique paths, no queue overlap.\\n- Shell syntax, workflow lint, aggregate diff check, and worktree cleanliness pass.\\n\\nMetadata caveat: remote PR123/PR124 heads and `main` bases intentionally remain at their pre-submit state until exact-head local gates finish. Local stack inference reports the correct bases with `needsRebase:false`; this is an expected submission gate, not a structural defect. The position-95 queue is also intentionally a historical checkpoint, so it does not record the subsequently created final commit IDs.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Core source behavior is clean for authorization, tenant isolation, direct-link outcomes, template structure, and announcement targeting.\\n\\nOne confirmed defect remains:\\n\\n- `events:viewPublic` is still presented as a configurable permission in `src/shared/permissions/permissions.ts`, but no runtime path enforces it. Remove this misleading no-op permission and its seed/test references.\\n\\nStack caveat:\\n\\n- The discovery commit removes `unlisted` and old listing permissions while Playwright/generated-documentation sources still reference them. The planned replacement patch must directly follow or be folded into that slice; otherwise intermediate PRs are not independently full-suite compliant.\\n\\nAll patches satisfy review limits: 3/23/34/33 files and 100/113/740/1,242 changed lines.\\n\\nRemaining proof gaps are PostgreSQL-backed discovery/role-transition checks and Browser/Playwright verification of direct-link and announcement journeys.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr_submission_manifest\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only live manifest captured on 2026-08-06:\\n\\n- Trunk: `main` at `d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea`\\n- Current/top branch: `codex/staging-latency-runbooks`\\n- Layers: 99\\n- `needsRebase`: false for all layers\\n- Only overlapping remote branches are the old heads for #123 and #124.\\n- Only existing PRs among all 99 branch names are:\\n  - #123 at position 95, open and ready, remote head `951cb9da6f51a785b1f41b1e73279aec3d0c882f`\\n  - #124 at position 99, open and re