{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T08:36:40.330Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019fd637-ab0a-7942-8d5d-0b10a47a6e98","author":"/root/acceptance_manifest","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/acceptance_manifest\nPayload:\nRead-only acceptance manifest complete. No tests or Browser sessions were run.\n\n### Authoritative status\n\n`APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md` is a pre-final checkpoint: RQ-003–RQ-012 and RQ-015 remain in progress, and historical pass counts are explicitly non-current evidence. Final proof must come from the actual integrated tip. See [APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md:73), [pending evidence](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md:1102), and [completion state](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md:1277).\n\n### Final-tip Playwright manifest\n\nRun the canonical commands without forwarded file/project/grep filters:\n\n| Command | Projects and purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `bun run test:e2e` | `database-setup → setup → local-chrome-baseline`; all 45 functional specs except external-provider-tagged tests. |\n| `bun run test:e2e:docs` | `database-setup → setup → docs-baseline`; baseline generated guides. |\n| `AUTH0_MANAGEMENT_CLIENT_ID=... AUTH0_MANAGEMENT_CLIENT_SECRET=... PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=... bun run test:e2e:integration` | `local-chrome-integration` + `docs-integration`; Auth0 Management account creation and live Google Maps autocomplete/persistence. |\n| `E2E_LIVE_ESN_CARD_IDENTIFIER=... E2E_LIVE_ESN_CARD_EXPIRED_IDENTIFIER=... bun run test:e2e:live-esncard:release` | Provider-error unit check plus `local-chrome-live-esncard` + `docs-live-esncard`; active and permanently expired ESNcard journeys. |\n| `EVORTO_PAGES_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/evorto-pages ... bun run test:e2e:docs:publish` | Aggregates `docs-baseline`, `docs-integration`, and `docs-live-esncard`, then transactionally synchronizes Pages. This mutates the Pages checkout and is only for intentional publication. |\n\nThe eight configured projects are `database-setup`, `setup`, `local-chrome-baseline`, `docs-baseline`, `local-chrome-integration`, `docs-integration`, `local-chrome-live-esncard`, and `docs-live-esncard`: [playwright.config.ts](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/playwright.config.ts:134). Scripts are defined in [package.json](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/package.json:26); the exact documented command forms are in [tests/README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:169). The full provider gate requires the integration command followed by the ESNcard release command: [README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/README.md:131).\n\nRelevant durable coverage already exists:\n\n- Discovery and announcements: `event-discovery-eligibility.test.ts`, `event-discovery.doc.ts`, `announcement-discovery.doc.ts`.\n- Transfers/payments: `registration-transfer.spec.ts` and `registration-transfer.doc.ts`; fixed bundle, recipient-current pricing, Checkout, exact source refunds, terminal failure and requeue. It remains candidate evidence until the full final-tip gate passes: [tests/test-inventory.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/test-inventory.md:227).\n- Settings/profile: `general-settings.spec.ts`, `general-settings.doc.ts`, routed profile specs/docs for overview, events, discounts, receipts, and editing.\n- Receipts/finance: `receipts-flows.spec.ts`, finance permissions, submission/review/reimbursement guides.\n- Scanning: `scanner.test.ts`, check-in and add-on-fulfillment guides.\n- Providers: Auth0 and Google Maps integration projects plus dedicated ESNcard projects: [tests/test-inventory.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/test-inventory.md:296).\n\n### Highest-value branch-authentic Browser journeys\n\n1. **SSR, discovery, direct links, announcements**\n\n   - Hard-load anonymous Events and confirm clean SSR→hydration, no authenticated-data flash, and normal navigation.\n   - Verify anonymous discovery uses only default-member-role sign-up choices and exposes only public event information.\n   - Open an event absent from the anonymous list by direct link: show the explicit sign-in state without restricted choices or false “information-only” copy.\n   - Signed in, verify any eligible choice makes an ordinary event discoverable and an ineligible direct link explains why.\n   - As admin, select an announcement role; as matching/nonmatching members, verify list visibility. Remove all roles and confirm link-only access. The selection must not imply access assignment or message delivery.\n\n2. **Participant, transfer, payment, profile**\n\n   - Traverse free registration, paid Checkout, waitlist join/leave, cancellation, ticket/QR, and receipt states from normal navigation.\n   - With source and recipient sessions, create and claim a private transfer via link/manual code. Inspect fixed-bundle details, recipient-current questions/pricing, free immediate completion, paid pending/success, and source refund/recovery copy.\n   - Navigate `/profile`, `/profile/events`, `/profile/discounts`, and `/profile/receipts`; verify routed focus handoff, status/action clarity, edit persistence, payment continuation, transferred-ticket loss, and submitted receipts.\n\n3. **Focused tenant settings**\n\n   - Walk Admin Settings through organization, registration, appearance, legal, and payments pages.\n   - Confirm independent saves, dirty-navigation confirmation, hydration/readiness, visible provider failures, and that payments require the separate payment-management permission. Routes and guards are in [admin.routes.ts](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/src/app/admin/admin.routes.ts:65).\n\n4. **Receipts and finance**\n\n   - Organizer: Events → Organize → Add receipt; exercise invalid file/breakdown recovery, successful PDF upload, organizer card, then Profile → Receipts.\n   - Finance admin: preview the exact receipt, approve it, and record reimbursement. Confirm the UI clearly states that Evorto records the reimbursement but does not transfer money.\n   - Exercise missing-evidence behavior: approval blocked, reasoned rejection still available.\n   - Verify finance/tax routes are absent or denied without the matching capability.\n\n5. **Scanner/check-in**\n\n   - Open Scanner without capability and confirm no camera request.\n   - With capability, inspect camera-ready and permission-denied/retry states.\n   - Use a deterministic registration-result URL to check in attendee plus guests, then a later guest arrival; confirm organizer totals.\n   - Redeem one add-on, undo immediately, and inspect cancellation/refund choices and explicit unavailable states.\n\n6. **Provider and platform-admin UI**\n\n   - Auth0 login/new-account/onboarding, including callback/hydration behavior.\n   - Live Google Maps place selection and reload persistence.\n   - ESNcard active/expired add, refresh, remove, and provider-error retry UI.\n   - Platform tenant list/search/detail/create/edit, target-scoped event/template/user/finance/scanner operations, audit-log evidence, and explicit custom-domain/impersonation boundaries.\n\nThese are the repository’s own manual queue priorities: [QUALITY.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:201). Every journey should record click path, visible result, console/network state, and screenshots where material: [QUALITY.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:361).\n\n### Aggregation and remaining proof gaps\n\n- There is **no single local script** aggregating baseline functional, baseline docs, provider integration, live ESNcard, Pages publication, and Browser acceptance.\n- `E2E Baseline` aggregates baseline functional and docs in CI: [e2e-baseline.yml](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/e2e-baseline.yml:213).\n- `Production Provider Certification` aggregates integration then ESNcard release certification: [esncard-release-certification.yml](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/esncard-release-certification.yml:245).\n- `test:e2e:docs:publish` aggregates all documentation projects: [publish-documentation.ts](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/publish-documentation.ts:18).\n- `test:e2e:ui` is exploratory baseline UI mode, not final gate evidence.\n\nStill missing on the actual final tip:\n\n- Complete PostgreSQL 17 concurrency proof for event roles, registration/payment/transfer, tenant, receipts, and email.\n- All canonical Playwright/provider/publication commands above with zero incomplete outcomes.\n- Exact Pages audit/build and neutral-image crop inspection.\n- Separate branch-authentic in-app Browser evidence; Playwright/screenshots cannot substitute.\n- Physical-device camera focus/QR recognition remains explicitly uncertified by mocked Playwright camera coverage: [tests/README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:59).\n- Stripe coverage is test-mode workflow evidence, not live bank/card-network settlement certification: [tests/README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:65).\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
