{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T09:11:38.858Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a744fc983ec8191aa4563839060b784","status":"completed","call_id":"call_FHMXb4hZYXR2fVyLeWddxngP","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh stack --help && gh stack edit --help 2>/dev/null || true && gh stack rebase --help 2>/dev/null || true && git town --version && git town sync --help | sed -n '1,180p'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":16000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T09:11:39.187Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd657-b1b3-7893-87a7-0310f33c7000","call_id":"call_FHMXb4hZYXR2fVyLeWddxngP","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Stacked PRs let you break a large change into a chain of pull requests\nthat build on each other. Use `gh stack` to create and manage your stack\nlocally, then push to GitHub to create your stack of PRs.\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack [command]\n\nExamples:\n  # Start a new stack targeting your default branch\n  $ gh stack init\n\n  # Or turn an existing set of branches into a stack\n  $ gh stack init branch1 branch2 branch3\n\n  # Make changes and commit, then add a branch to the stack\n  $ gh stack add branch4\n\n  # Push all branches and create/update PRs on GitHub\n  $ gh stack submit\n\n  # Keep your local in sync with remote\n  $ gh stack sync\n\nStack management:\n  add         Add a new branch on top of the current stack\n  checkout    Checkout a stack by stack number, PR number, PR URL, or branch name\n  init        Initialize a new stack\n  modify      Interactively restructure a stack\n  unstack     Remove a stack locally and on GitHub\n  view        View the current stack\n\nRemote operations:\n  link        Link PRs into a stack on GitHub without local tracking\n  merge       Merge a stack of pull requests\n  push        Push active branches in the current stack to the remote\n  rebase      Rebase a stack of branches\n  submit      Create a stack of PRs on GitHub\n  sync        Sync the current stack with the remote\n\nNavigation:\n  bottom      Check out the bottom branch of the stack (closest to the trunk)\n  down        Check out a branch further down in the stack (closer to the trunk)\n  switch      Interactively switch to another branch in the stack\n  top         Check out the top branch of the stack (furthest from the trunk)\n  trunk       Check out the trunk branch of the stack\n  up          Check out a branch further up in the stack (further from the trunk)\n\nUtilities:\n  alias       Create a shell alias for gh stack\n  feedback    Submit feedback for gh-stack\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help      help for stack\n  -v, --version   version for stack\n\nUse \"gh stack [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nLearn more:\n  Documentation: https://gh.io/stacks\n  Feedback: https://gh.io/stacks-feedback\nStacked PRs let you break a large change into a chain of pull requests\nthat build on each other. Use `gh stack` to create and manage your stack\nlocally, then push to GitHub to create your stack of PRs.\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack [command]\n\nExamples:\n  # Start a new stack targeting your default branch\n  $ gh stack init\n\n  # Or turn an existing set of branches into a stack\n  $ gh stack init branch1 branch2 branch3\n\n  # Make changes and commit, then add a branch to the stack\n  $ gh stack add branch4\n\n  # Push all branches and create/update PRs on GitHub\n  $ gh stack submit\n\n  # Keep your local in sync with remote\n  $ gh stack sync\n\nStack management:\n  add         Add a new branch on top of the current stack\n  checkout    Checkout a stack by stack number, PR number, PR URL, or branch name\n  init        Initialize a new stack\n  modify      Interactively restructure a stack\n  unstack     Remove a stack locally and on GitHub\n  view        View the current stack\n\nRemote operations:\n  link        Link PRs into a stack on GitHub without local tracking\n  merge       Merge a stack of pull requests\n  push        Push active branches in the current stack to the remote\n  rebase      Rebase a stack of branches\n  submit      Create a stack of PRs on GitHub\n  sync        Sync the current stack with the remote\n\nNavigation:\n  bottom      Check out the bottom branch of the stack (closest to the trunk)\n  down        Check out a branch further down in the stack (closer to the trunk)\n  switch      Interactively switch to another branch in the stack\n  top         Check out the top branch of the stack (furthest from the trunk)\n  trunk       Check out the trunk branch of the stack\n  up          Check out a branch further up in the stack (further from the trunk)\n\nUtilities:\n  alias       Create a shell alias for gh stack\n  feedback    Submit feedback for gh-stack\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help      help for stack\n  -v, --version   version for stack\n\nUse \"gh stack [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nLearn more:\n  Documentation: https://gh.io/stacks\n  Feedback: https://gh.io/stacks-feedback\nPull from remote and do a cascading rebase across the stack.\n\nEnsures that each branch in the stack has the tip of the previous\nlayer in its commit history, rebasing if necessary.\n\nUse --no-trunk to skip fetching and rebasing with the trunk branch.\nOnly the inter-branch rebases are performed (branch 2 onto branch 1,\nbranch 3 onto branch 2, etc.).\n\nUsage:\n  gh stack rebase [branch] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  # Rebase the entire stack\n  $ gh stack rebase\n\n  # Only rebase from trunk to the current branch\n  $ gh stack rebase --downstack\n\n  # Only rebase from current branch to the top\n  $ gh stack rebase --upstack\n\n  # Rebase stack branches without pulling from or rebasing with trunk\n  $ gh stack rebase --no-trunk\n\n  # Continue after resolving conflicts\n  $ gh stack rebase --continue\n\n  # Abort and restore all branches\n  $ gh stack rebase --abort\n\nFlags:\n      --abort                           Abort rebase and restore all branches\n      --committer-date-is-author-date   Set the committer date to the author date during rebase\n      --continue                        Continue rebase after resolving conflicts\n      --downstack                       Only rebase branches from trunk to current branch\n  -h, --help                            help for rebase\n      --no-trunk                        Skip trunk — only rebase stack branches onto each other\n      --preserve-dates                  Alias for --committer-date-is-author-date\n      --remote string                   Remote to fetch from (defaults to auto-detected remote)\n      --upstack                         Only rebase branches from current branch to top\nGit Town 22.4.0\nUpdate the current branch with all relevant changes.\n\nSynchronizes the current branch with the rest of the world.\n\nWhen run on a feature branch:\n- syncs all ancestor branches\n- pulls updates for the current branch\n- merges the parent branch into the current branch\n- pushes the current branch\n- updates branch lineage in proposals\n\nWhen run on the main branch or a perennial branch:\n- pulls and pushes updates for the current branch\n- pushes tags\n\nIf the repository contains an \"upstream\" remote, syncs the main branch with its upstream counterpart. You can disable this by running \"git config git-town.sync-upstream false\".\n\nUsage:\n  git-town sync [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --all               sync all local branches\n      --auto-resolve      auto-resolve phantom merge conflicts\n  -d, --detached          don't update the perennial root branch\n      --dry-run           print but do not run the Git commands\n      --gone              sync only branches whose remote is gone\n  -h, --help              help for sync\n      --no-auto-resolve   don't auto-resolve\n      --no-detached       disable detached\n      --no-push           don't push branches\n  -p, --prune             prune empty branches\n      --push              push local branches\n  -s, --stack             sync the stack that the current branch belongs to\n  -v, --verbose           display all Git commands run under the hood\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
