{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T09:23:01.179Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019fd662-19ba-7bc3-add7-8d346c83a186","call_id":"call_C9baEG3vHpowSo9CQlSIJr3R","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_82_99\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/complete_manifest\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/complete_manifest/metadata_tree_check\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Core source behavior is clean for authorization, tenant isolation, direct-link outcomes, template structure, and announcement targeting.\\n\\nOne confirmed defect remains:\\n\\n- `events:viewPublic` is still presented as a configurable permission in `src/shared/permissions/permissions.ts`, but no runtime path enforces it. Remove this misleading no-op permission and its seed/test references.\\n\\nStack caveat:\\n\\n- The discovery commit removes `unlisted` and old listing permissions while Playwright/generated-documentation sources still reference them. The planned replacement patch must directly follow or be folded into that slice; otherwise intermediate PRs are not independently full-suite compliant.\\n\\nAll patches satisfy review limits: 3/23/34/33 files and 100/113/740/1,242 changed lines.\\n\\nRemaining proof gaps are PostgreSQL-backed discovery/role-transition checks and Browser/Playwright verification of direct-link and announcement journeys.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/final_ci_gate_manifest\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Current source requires the full canonical baseline on every one of the 99 exact PR heads—not only on the integrated tip. Any rebase or assembly change invalidates evidence for that SHA.\\n\\n### Per-head mandatory order\\n\\nRun this exact, unfiltered sequence from [README.md:97](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/README.md:97):\\n\\n```bash\\nbun install --frozen-lockfile\\nbun run release:validate\\nbun run format:write\\nbun run format:check\\nbun run lint\\ngit diff --exit-code\\ntest -z \\\"$(git status --porcelain=v1)\\\"\\nbun run test:unit:server\\nbun run test:unit\\nbun run test:integration:postgres:local\\nbun run build:app\\nbun run infra:check\\nbun run image:security:local\\nbun run test:e2e\\nbun run test:e2e:docs\\n```\\n\\nWhy this is per head:\\n\\n- PR Quality has an unfiltered `pull_request` trigger and requires PostgreSQL, code quality, Terraform, and image security to all succeed: [pr-quality.yml:3](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/pr-quality.yml:3), [pr-quality.yml:274](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/pr-quality.yml:274).\\n- Repository policy requires every triggered suite locally before any PR update: [AGENTS.md:146](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/AGENTS.md:146), [QUALITY.md:243](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:243).\\n- The root README additionally defines functional and docs E2E as part of the “normal pull-request baseline,” despite E2E Baseline itself being main-push-only.\\n\\nTherefore the existing per-head harness is incomplete unless it adds:\\n\\n```bash\\nbun run test:integration:postgres:local\\nbun run infra:check\\nbun run image:security:local\\nbun run test:e2e\\nbun run test:e2e:docs\\n```\\n\\nIt must also add the two clean-tree assertions. “Format write as required” should become unconditional `format:write` followed by `format:check`.\\n\\n`bun run test:e2e:install` is a setup prerequisite whenever Playwright’s browser cache is missing or its version changed; CI installs Chromium before browser-backed server tests: [tests/README.md:410](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:410), [pr-quality.yml:144](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/pr-quality.yml:144).\\n\\n### Final integrated/conditional gates\\n\\nProvider certification, in this order:\\n\\n```bash\\nbun run test:e2e:integration\\nbun run test:e2e:live-esncard:release\\n```\\n\\nThese require the baseline environment plus Auth0 Management credentials, Google Maps key, and the active/permanently-expired ESNcard identifiers. They are not triggered by an ordinary PR push; the provider workflow is manual/reusable and Release invokes it only after a merged `knope/release` PR: [esncard-release-certification.yml:3](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/esncard-release-certification.yml:3), [release.yml:3](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/release.yml:3).\\n\\nDocumentation publication:\\n\\n```bash\\nEVORTO_PAGES_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/clean-current-update-checkout \\\\\\n  bun run test:e2e:docs:publish\\n```\\n\\nThen, in Evorto Pages:\\n\\n```bash\\nbun run test:docs-tooling\\nbun run lint\\nbun run build\\n```\\n\\nThe tooling audit is required because this stack changes the publication contract. Publication runs all three docs projects and atomically mutates the Pages generated guide/assets trees: [publish-documentation.ts:283](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/publish-documentation.ts:283), [publish-documentation.ts:309](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/publish-documentation.ts:309).\\n\\nBlocker: [Evorto Pages README:65](/Users/hedde/code/evorto-pages/README.md:65) requires a clean, current `update` checkout. The discovered checkouts are currently `codex/plain-language-doc-slugs` and `master`; neither is `update`.\\n\\nBranch-authentic in-app Browser acceptance remains separate. Playwright cannot substitute for it: [QUALITY.md:85](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:85).\\n\\n### Docker lifecycle ordering\\n\\nUse:\\n\\n```bash\\nbun run docker:check\\nbun run docker:start\\nbun run docker:ps\\n# Require HTTP 204 from $BASE_URL/readyz\\n\\nnode_modules/.bin/dotenv -c dev -- \\\\\\n  docker compose stop db minio mailpit stripe worker evorto\\n\\nbun run docker:resume\\nbun run docker:ps\\n# Require HTTP 204 again\\nbun run docker:stop\\n```\\n\\nDo not use `docker:stop` before testing resume: it executes `docker compose down` and removes containers, while resume requires their existing IDs: [docker-stack.sh:120](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/docker-stack.sh:120), [docker-resume.sh:61](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/docker-resume.sh:61).\\n\\nFor empty-volume proof, use a fresh isolated Compose project and canonical E2E. The disposable wrapper removes and verifies all project containers, networks, and volumes on exit: [docker-webserver.sh:37](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/docker-webserver.sh:37).\\n\\n### Environment and mutation cautions\\n\\n- Required baseline: Bun 1.3.14, Node 24.15.0, Docker Compose ≥2.24, Chromium, `FONT_AWESOME_TOKEN`, Auth0 app configuration and six test passwords, session secret, Stripe test configuration, and local PostgreSQL 17/MinIO/Mailpit/Stripe services.\\n- PostgreSQL integration drops/recreates only the disposable `evorto_postgres_integration` public schema: [tests/README.md:199](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:199).\\n- `format:write` and `lint` can change tracked files; `build:app` writes `dist/`; runtime/E2E/image scripts generate `.env.dev`; Playwright writes ignored `test-results`; Docker commands reset databases and mutate Docker state.\\n- `image:security:local` builds/removes an image and creates source-map/SBOM temporaries. `infra:check` and release validation may populate user tool caches.\\n- Module guidance adds no distinct test command, but repeats lint/format and requests sequential WebStorm diagnostics on edited non-Markdown files when possible.\\n\\nOther workflows add no ordinary branch-push local gate: Git Town only displays stack metadata; Copilot Setup is path-limited and unchanged; E2E and staging are main-only/downstream; production and staging reset are manual; latency is scheduled/manual.\\n\\n\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
