{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:28:05.312Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The host evidence is now clear: the failing run used the default 13-way worker pool while two unrelated, day-old processes continuously occupied two cores and the machine’s load was above 20; the test runner then spent most of its time starting/importing workers, not executing tests. I’m keeping those unrelated projects untouched. The safe correction is to cap the test pool while still collecting every test and to preserve installed dependencies between branch heads so repeated clean installs do not provoke the same filesystem/security-scanner pressure.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
