{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:29:46.618Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"A second independent review confirms the same diagnosis: the failed check is a synchronous repository scan that normally completes in 4.7 seconds but crossed its 5-second limit under pressure, while two whole test files never obtained workers. I’m leaving the canonical commands unchanged. The rerun will be exclusive, will begin only after the transient host pressure clears, and the harness will retain dependencies between heads while still performing the required frozen install on each one.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
