{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:32:15.905Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019fd6a1-7f21-7463-abeb-eadae369fa21","call_id":"call_XVrwrk927MRXtfjn58vAUtix","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27/failure_log_analysis\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Strongest diagnosis: transient host/Vitest fork-pool starvation, not a source regression.\\n\\n- Same immutable head `3c1ea2e…` and command passed previously: 182 files, 1,451 tests, 52.32s.\\n- Current run: 180 files, 1,431 tests, 1 timeout, 2 worker-start errors, 1,020.54s.\\n- The missing 20 tests exactly equal the two workers that never started:\\n  - `publish-documentation.spec.ts`: 13 tests\\n  - `esncard-release-source.spec.ts`: 7 tests\\n- Transform/import time exploded from `32.33s / 459.98s` to `2978.11s / 8175.57s`, while aggregate test-body time fell from `107.99s` to `81.87s`.\\n- The source scan previously passed in 4,684ms, then exceeded the 5,000ms timeout by only 265ms. Earlier parallel audits show the same timeout signature, followed by a serialized pass.\\n- Current exit was `1`, not wrapper timeout `124`; no process-kill signal appears.\\n\\nEvidence:\\n\\n- Current failure: `/tmp/evorto-full-baseline-1-27.xuvFj0/logs/001_unit_server.log`\\n- Current events/failure: `/tmp/evorto-full-baseline-1-27.xuvFj0/events.json`, `/tmp/evorto-full-baseline-1-27.xuvFj0/failure.json`\\n- Archived same-head success: `/tmp/evorto-full-baseline-1-27.xuvFj0/attempt-1-missing-postgres-prereq/logs/001_unit_server.log`\\n- Corroborating parallel failures: `/tmp/evorto-gates-28-54.3mSb63/logs/p28_34/28-test-unit-server.log`, `p35_44/35-test-unit-server.log`, `p45_54/45-test-unit-server.log`\\n- Later serialized pass: `/tmp/evorto-gates-28-54.3mSb63/logs/p28_34/29-test-unit-server.log`\\n\\nArtifact warning: root `unit_all` and integration logs/counts are stale from attempt 1; their mtimes are 11:59, while current events stop at `unit_server`. Only `counts/001_unit_server.counts.txt` is current.\\n\\nSafe next steps:\\n\\n- Archive this failed attempt before another run.\\n- Keep future artifacts attempt-scoped.\\n- Serialize heavy baseline work and wait for Vitest/Angular/lint/build/image jobs and host load to settle.\\n- Preserve the exact canonical command and require fresh approval before restarting.\\n- Do not increase timeouts or alter worker concurrency; that would mask the failure and change the evidence.\\n\\nNo tests were rerun and no files were edited.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27/host_pressure\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only diagnosis complete and corrected to the 12:08–12:25 failure.\\n\\nThe proximate failure was a transient Vitest fork-worker stall plus a near-threshold 5-second test. Broad ~3× gate slowdown and elevated post-run load make host contention plausible, but there is no evidence of acute memory, process-limit, disk, thermal, or Docker exhaustion. Two unrelated Window Watcher Node processes consumed two cores throughout both the failed and earlier successful runs, so they may exacerbate contention but do not fully explain it.\\n\\nNo tests or services were started, no processes were signaled, and no files were edited.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27/unit_failure_source\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Diagnosis sent to the parent with exact file/log evidence.\\n\\nConclusion: transient worker/resource starvation, not a deterministic branch defect. The identical head previously passed; the scan test merely has unsafe timing margin—4.684s against Vitest’s 5s default—and should later receive scoped hardening. No tests were run and no files or artifacts were modified.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_82_99\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Core source behavior is clean for authorization, tenant isolation, direct-link outcomes, template structure, and announcement targeting.\\n\\nOne confirmed defect remains:\\n\\n- `events:viewPublic` is still presented as a configurable permission in `src/shared/permissions/permissions.ts`, but no runtime path enforces it. Remove this misleading no-op permission and its seed/test references.\\n\\nStack caveat:\\n\\n- The discovery commit removes `unlisted` and old listing permissions while Playwright/generated-documentation sources still reference them. The planned replacement patch must directly follow or be folded into that slice; otherwise intermediate PRs are not independently full-suite compliant.\\n\\nAll patches satisfy review limits: 3/23/34/33 files and 100/113/740/1,242 changed lines.\\n\\nRemaining proof gaps are PostgreSQL-backed discovery/role-transition checks and Browser/Playwright verification of direct-link and announcement journeys.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
