{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:41:38.620Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The security scan is a normal multi-module macOS cycle, not a stuck Evorto process; it has moved from Pirrit to Adload to WaterNet. Waiting for every module is unnecessary on a 14-core machine. I’m making the setup deterministic instead: the official commands stay unchanged, every test remains collected, but Vitest is explicitly limited to eight workers and the run records that setting. Combined with the host-wide lock and load preflight, this removes the worker-start starvation without extending timeouts or hiding failures.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:41:38.620Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a7464e0f80881918d67274dc38eec6d","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The security scan is a normal multi-module macOS cycle, not a stuck Evorto process; it has moved from Pirrit to Adload to WaterNet. Waiting for every module is unnecessary on a 14-core machine. I’m making the setup deterministic instead: the official commands stay unchanged, every test remains collected, but Vitest is explicitly limited to eight workers and the run records that setting. Combined with the host-wide lock and load preflight, this removes the worker-start starvation without extending timeouts or hiding failures."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:41:41.953Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a7464e2a36c8191baf71c1eff5a274d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_Su5XCirXphvBf0kyHbbq6r0Y","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: ../../../../../../tmp/evorto-full-baseline-1-27.xuvFj0/run-full-baseline.sh\\n@@\\n export NO_COLOR=1\\n export FORCE_COLOR=0\\n export TERM=dumb\\n export BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=\\\"$audit_root/bun-cache\\\"\\n+export VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=8\\n@@\\n-  local cpu_count load_1m xprotect_cpu heavy_processes\\n+  local cpu_count load_1m xprotect_cpu heavy_processes\\n@@\\n     --argjson load_1m \\\"$load_1m\\\" \\\\\\n     --argjson xprotect_cpu \\\"$xprotect_cpu\\\" \\\\\\n+    --argjson vitest_max_workers \\\"$VITEST_MAX_WORKERS\\\" \\\\\\n     --arg heavy_processes \\\"$heavy_processes\\\" \\\\\\n-    '{recorded_at:$recorded_at,cpu_count:$cpu_count,load_1m:$load_1m,xprotect_cpu_percent:$xprotect_cpu,other_heavy_processes:($heavy_processes | split(\\\"\\\\n\\\") | map(select(length > 0)))}' \\\\\\n+    '{recorded_at:$recorded_at,cpu_count:$cpu_count,load_1m:$load_1m,xprotect_cpu_percent:$xprotect_cpu,vitest_max_workers:$vitest_max_workers,other_heavy_processes:($heavy_processes | split(\\\"\\\\n\\\") | map(select(length > 0)))}' \\\\\\n@@\\n-  if ! awk -v cpu=\\\"$xprotect_cpu\\\" 'BEGIN { exit !(cpu <= 10) }'; then\\n-    printf 'Refusing to start while the macOS security scanner is active at %.1f%% CPU.\\\\n' \\\\\\n-      \\\"$xprotect_cpu\\\" >&2\\n-    return 1\\n-  fi\\n }\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
