{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T10:53:48.158Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The Docker evidence points to the engine boundary, not PostgreSQL or the project: Compose created the network, volume, and container, Docker Desktop approved the mount and port, then no container-start request reached the Linux daemon. Its backend was also emitting repeated event-stream EOFs. I’ve captured a full Docker diagnostic bundle. I’m now restarting Docker Desktop itself; the three unrelated running containers are protected by `unless-stopped`/`always` policies and I’ll verify they return before touching the isolated failed project.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
