{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T11:01:16.324Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019fd6bc-0da4-79c1-8c53-2c649cfdaae1","author":"/root/timeout_wrapper_fix","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/timeout_wrapper_fix\nPayload:\nDiagnosis sent to the coordinator. The worktree remains unchanged and clean.\n\nKey conclusion: `EPERM` is neither “group gone” nor ordinary “group alive.” It means cleanup cannot be fully verified or controlled. Handle it only at the post-exit probe, emit a clear warning, cancel the futile force-kill timer, and preserve the intended `130`, `143`, or `124` outcome. Unexpected errors should still fail loudly."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
