{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T11:25:37.512Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019fd6d2-5968-7523-a138-a315ef8f7561","call_id":"call_Ej25TseoUbfwtHimVLPs9Iq3","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54/inspect_70_73\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81/split_82_84\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/complete_manifest/manifest_1_50\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Pos38 and pos44 have safe mandatory splits. Pos47 should remain a cohesive exception: a whole-file split would leave an invalid operational/test intermediate head.\\n\\n## Position 38 — mandatory two-way split\\n\\n1. `codex/make-platform-ticket-lookup-explicit`  \\n   Title: `fix: make platform ticket lookup explicit`  \\n   7 files, +125/-249 = 374 lines.\\n\\n   Whole-file group:\\n\\n   - `helpers/testing/platform-authority-source.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/app/global-admin/platform-event-operations/platform-scanner.component.html`\\n   - `src/app/global-admin/platform-event-operations/platform-scanner.component.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/app/global-admin/platform-event-operations/platform-scanner.component.ts`\\n   - `src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/platform/platform-registrations.handlers.ts`\\n   - `src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/platform/platform.handlers.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/shared/rpc-contracts/app-rpcs/platform-events.rpcs.ts`\\n\\n   Keep the contract, handler removal, platform component, and tests together: the component stops calling the removed list operation in this layer. It also owns the platform lookup-navigation retry state.\\n\\n2. `codex/make-member-scanner-recovery-explicit`  \\n   Title: `fix: make member scanner recovery explicit`  \\n   4 files, +627/-77 = 704 lines.\\n\\n   Whole-file group:\\n\\n   - `.changeset/make-scanner-recovery-explicit.md`\\n   - `src/app/scanning/scanner/scanner.component.html`\\n   - `src/app/scanning/scanner/scanner.component.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/app/scanning/scanner/scanner.component.ts`\\n\\n   This keeps camera authorization, lifecycle handling, explicit retry states, template, and component tests together. The 704-line child is a justified near-target cohesive unit; splitting its implementation and specification would weaken the intermediate head.\\n\\nNo hunk split is required.\\n\\n## Position 44 — mandatory three-way split\\n\\n1. `codex/harden-auth-session-runtime`  \\n   Title: `fix: harden authentication session runtime`  \\n   4 files, +443/-193 = 636 lines.\\n\\n   Whole-file group:\\n\\n   - `.changeset/harden-auth0-cookie-boundary.md`\\n   - `src/server/auth/auth-session.ts`\\n   - `src/server/config/auth-config.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/server/config/auth-config.ts`\\n\\n   Auth configuration and session implementation must move together because the configuration changes secrets to redacted values consumed by the session runtime. The complete config specification must also move here because the parent tests use secrets that become invalid under the new minimum-length rule.\\n\\n2. `codex/prove-auth-session-boundaries`  \\n   Title: `test: prove authentication session boundaries`  \\n   2 files, +189/-7 = 196 lines.\\n\\n   Whole-file group:\\n\\n   - `src/app/core/auth-token.interceptor.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/server/auth/auth-session.spec.ts`\\n\\n   These tests depend on the new cookie identifiers and exported session helpers from child 1. Keeping them separate provides a focused proof layer without leaving child 1 incompatible with its pre-existing tests.\\n\\n3. `codex/make-identity-authority-explicit`  \\n   Title: `fix: make identity authority explicit`  \\n   9 files, +170/-71 = 241 lines.\\n\\n   Whole-file group:\\n\\n   - `.changeset/harden-identity-authority-boundaries.md`\\n   - `.changeset/remove-legacy-identity-authority.md`\\n   - `src/server/config/deployment-config.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/server/config/deployment-config.ts`\\n   - `src/server/config/test-runtime-config.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/server/config/test-runtime-config.ts`\\n   - `src/server/context/http-request-context.ts`\\n   - `src/server/context/request-context-resolver.spec.ts`\\n   - `src/server/context/request-context-resolver.ts`\\n\\n   Deployment/test configuration must stay with request-context resolution because the resolver now consumes explicitly parsed local test-authority IDs. This layer atomically removes ambient process-state and legacy metadata authority.\\n\\nNo hunk split is required.\\n\\n## Position 47 — retain as cohesive exception\\n\\nRetain:\\n\\n- Branch: `codex/cut-over-hosting-environment-state`\\n- Title: `infra: cut over Scaleway environment state`\\n- 24 files, +609/-889 = 1,498 lines.\\n\\nWhole-file group:\\n\\n- `.changeset/isolate-scaleway-terraform-state.md`\\n- `.github/workflows/scaleway-production.yml`\\n- `.github/workflows/scaleway-staging-reset.yml`\\n- `.github/workflows/scaleway-staging.yml`\\n- `helpers/testing/scaleway-hosting-source.spec.ts`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/.terraform.lock.hcl`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/backend.hcl.example`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/dns.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/main.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/modules/environment/containers.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/modules/environment/outputs.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/modules/environment/storage.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/modules/environment/variables.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/outputs.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/production/dns.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/production/main.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/production/outputs.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/staging/dns.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/staging/main.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/staging/outputs.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/terraform.tfvars.example`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/transactional-email.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/variables.tf`\\n- `infrastructure/scaleway/versions.tf`\\n\\nWhy it is atomic:\\n\\n- The environment module removes internally owned registry/IAM resources and outputs while adding required bootstrap-owned application inputs.\\n- The new staging and production roots require that new module interface.\\n- The old combined root supplies the removed input and reads removed outputs, so it cannot coexist with the final module changes.\\n- The workflows change root paths, state credentials, and environment-specific variables together.\\n- `scaleway-hosting-source.spec.ts` replaces cross-cutting assertions spanning the root layout, module interface, workflows, state credentials, DNS, database variables, and storage authority.\\n\\nA nominal whole-file split would be 889 lines for Terraform plus the changeset, followed by 609 lines for workflows and the source specification. The first head would retain stale workflows pointing at the deleted root and its unchanged source test would fail, so that is not an acceptable independently gated stack layer.\\n\\nIf a strict split is forced, it requires transient code and hunk-level restructuring rather than partitioning the current diff:\\n\\n- In `containers.tf`, `outputs.tf`, `storage.tf`, and module `variables.tf`, add the external-principal interface while temporarily retaining the old IAM/registry resources, inputs, and outputs.\\n- Temporarily adapt the old combined root to that compatibility interface before introducing the new roots.\\n- Split `scaleway-hosting-source.spec.ts` inside the `isolates every Terraform root`, PostgreSQL, and private-storage test blocks so root-layout assertions move before workflow-path, credential, and workflow-variable assertions.\\n- Cut workflows over only after both roots validate, then remove the old root and compatibility interface in a final cleanup layer.\\n\\nThose transient changes are absent from the reviewed final diff and increase state-migration risk, so the 1,498-line cohesive exception is safer.\\n\\nAll proposed new branch names were checked and are currently available. This was read-only inspection; no tests or mutations were performed.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/large_layer_human_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
