{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T11:47:46.185Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd6e6-9f89-7a12-8515-54dad6d15f1d","call_id":"call_vN9sADWihEdYVFPXmOw1qJMZ","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"67:- `test:e2e:docs:publish`, APP_HOST_PORT, `APP_HOST_PORT=${APP_HOST_PORT:-4200}`, Auth0, `Callback URL mismatch`, localhost:4560, `refs/heads/update`, publish-documentation.ts, e0275f533ff, parallel E2E\n79:- `test:e2e:docs:publish` must default `APP_HOST_PORT` in the script because `env:runtime` runs before dotenv loading. The publisher should require the Pages checkout to track `refs/heads/update` and validate the combined marketing path. [Task 2]\n83:- Symptom: generated worktree publication receives HTTP 403 `Callback URL mismatch` for `http://localhost:4560/callback`. Cause: Auth0 only registers port 4200 and `.env` is loaded too late. Fix: default `APP_HOST_PORT=${APP_HOST_PORT:-4200}` in the publication script, while allowing explicit overrides. [Task 2]\n1116:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/85ef/evorto, rollout_path=/Users/hedde/.codex/archived_sessions/rollout-2026-07-01T16-40-28-019f1e1f-cead-7703-8716-984c05bcb15a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-01T16:23:43+00:00, thread_id=019f1e1f-cead-7703-8716-984c05bcb15a, Browser reproduced the Auth0 callback mismatch and the allowed local port fix)\n1120:- Auth0 callback mismatch, APP_HOST_PORT=4200, http://localhost:4579/login, redirect_uri, docker:ps, Browser root check, page.evaluate read-only, auth fixture\n1154:- Authenticated local Browser/Playwright checks depend on the repo's out-of-band Auth0 callback setup; `tests/README.md` points to `APP_HOST_PORT=4200 bun run docker:start` unless the generated worktree port is already registered. [Task 1][Task 2]\n1155:- Browser reproduction at `http://localhost:4579/login` showing `Callback URL mismatch` means the callback port is wrong, not necessarily that app logic is broken. [Task 2]\n1160:- Final local verification that passed here was `bun run test:unit` -> `52 passed (295 tests)` plus `APP_HOST_PORT=4200 bun run test:e2e -- tests/specs/permissions/override.test.ts` -> `8 passed`. [Task 3]\n1166:- Symptom: Browser auth reproduction fails immediately on login. Cause: the local stack used a worktree-generated callback port not registered in Auth0. Fix: restart with `APP_HOST_PORT=4200` or another registered port before touching app code. [Task 2]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
