{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T11:50:31.740Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019fd6e9-263c-7482-b8f4-debe2ed75e6f","call_id":"call_CQWQ8or6O7rkrlxlvPhti1tK","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_1_27\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_28_54/inspect_70_73\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81/split_82_84\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Audited both exact first-parent diffs read-only. No tests were run.\\n\\n## `993235de…` — position 82\\n\\nParent: `9cc62767d925bc380f7ec89a06b3b3be99bd1eaf`  \\nTotal: `+692/-505 = 1,197` changed lines across 16 files.\\n\\nVerdict: mandatory split. It exceeds 700 lines and contains six independent journeys; no cohesive exception is defensible.\\n\\n1. `codex/82-member-role-administration`  \\n   `test: prove member role administration`  \\n   `+99/-78 = 177`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/roles/about-permissions.doc.ts` — 11\\n   - `tests/docs/roles/roles.doc.ts` — 135\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/roles-management.spec.ts` — 15\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/user-role-assignment.spec.ts` — 10\\n   - `tests/support/utils/user-role-assignment-scenario.ts` — 6\\n\\n2. `codex/82-member-onboarding`  \\n   `test: prove member onboarding`  \\n   `+56/-70 = 126`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/users/tenant-onboarding.doc.ts` — 126\\n\\n3. `codex/82-organization-settings`  \\n   `test: prove organization settings`  \\n   `+238/-158 = 396`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/general-settings.spec.ts` — 362\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/google-maps-location.spec.ts` — 8\\n   - `tests/specs/permissions/matrix.spec.ts` — 7\\n   - `tests/support/permissions/matrix.ts` — 19\\n\\n4. `codex/82-semantic-theme-contrast`  \\n   `test: prove semantic theme contrast`  \\n   `+106/-8 = 114`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/smoke/semantic-theme-colors.test.ts` — 114\\n\\n5. `codex/82-platform-tenant-administration`  \\n   `test: prove platform tenant administration`  \\n   `+114/-77 = 191`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/global-admin-tenants.spec.ts` — 132\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/platform-tenant-operations.spec.ts` — 35\\n   - `tests/specs/permissions/global-admin-route-guard.spec.ts` — 24\\n\\n6. `codex/82-email-delivery-administration`  \\n   `test: prove email delivery administration`  \\n   `+79/-114 = 193`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/email-outbox.spec.ts` — 86\\n   - `tests/support/utils/email-outbox-scenario.ts` — 107\\n\\nDependencies/order:\\n\\n- Files are disjoint between children. Shared data and consumer tests remain together.\\n- Keep the email child last. At `993235de…`, `EmailOutboxScenario` exposes only `failed`, `unknown`, `sending`, and `sent` at helper lines 17–22, while unchanged `tests/docs/admin/email-outbox.doc.ts:77-80,145` still accesses `queued`, `retry`, and `exhausted`.\\n- The following commit, `cc125768…`, repairs that documentation consumer. Therefore child 6 and the original unsplit position-82 commit are not typecheck/full-suite plausible in isolation.\\n- Children 1–5 are statically plausible individually, but full Playwright plausibility is low because untouched catch-up tests still target UI changed by earlier application commits. Targeted suites are the credible intermediate checks.\\n- No within-file split is recommended. Keep the complete `global admin route guard allow/deny path` suites in child 5, including Email delivery and audit routes, because they form one platform route-guard inventory. Keep the single multi-step general-settings test intact in child 3.\\n\\n## `909475f4…` — position 84\\n\\nParent: `cc125768705c784f20ab22862635d6b47654411c`  \\nTotal: `+615/-451 = 1,066` changed lines across 12 files.\\n\\nVerdict: mandatory split. It combines ESNcard, general profile, onboarding, and organizer receipt-form journeys.\\n\\n1. `codex/84-esncard-discount-journeys`  \\n   `test: prove ESNcard discount journeys`  \\n   `+353/-290 = 643`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts` — 325\\n   - `tests/specs/discounts/esn-discounts.test.ts` — 2\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-discounts.spec.ts` — 52\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-live-esncard.spec.ts` — 264\\n\\n2. `codex/84-profile-pages`  \\n   `test: prove profile pages`  \\n   `+221/-121 = 342`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/profile/user-profile.doc.ts` — 155\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-edit.spec.ts` — 16\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-events.spec.ts` — 21\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-receipts.spec.ts` — 12\\n   - `tests/support/utils/profile-event-cards.ts` — 138\\n\\n3. `codex/84-member-account-onboarding`  \\n   `test: prove member account onboarding`  \\n   `+37/-34 = 71`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/create-account.spec.ts` — 19\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/tenant-onboarding.spec.ts` — 52\\n\\n4. `codex/84-receipt-submission-controls`  \\n   `test: align receipt submission controls`  \\n   `+4/-6 = 10`\\n\\n   - `tests/support/utils/receipt-submission.ts` — 10\\n\\nDependencies/order:\\n\\n- Child 1 should be first: its parent’s `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts:12` imports the deleted `profile/user-profile/user-profile.esn-card` path; the actual module is already under `profile/profile-discounts/`.\\n- Static checks likely remain red until child 2. The parent schema requires `alcoholAmount`, `depositAmount`, `hasAlcohol`, `hasDeposit`, and a date-string `receiptDate`; child 2 updates the stale receipt inserts and profile-event fixture snapshots.\\n- Children 3 and 4 are runtime-selector/content alignments and have no code dependency on each other.\\n- Full suite plausibility starts only after all four. Child 1’s live ESNcard coverage additionally requires the credential-gated provider suite; non-live ESNcard tests are the plausible intermediate evidence.\\n- Child 4 must exercise its unchanged consumers: `tests/docs/finance/receipt-submission.doc.ts` and `tests/specs/finance/receipts-flows.spec.ts`.\\n- No within-file split is recommended. Keep the entire `Manage your profile` documentation test in child 2 because its shared setup/cleanup deliberately traverses overview, events, and receipts. Keep all three ESNcard documentation blocks—status, managed card, and live-provider flow—in child 1; the 643-line child remains below the limit and is one cohesive domain journey.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only split design is complete and sent to the coordinator.\\n\\nIt replaces the four oversized commits with 13 focused children, all under 100 files and projected below roughly 700 changed lines. Required hunk splits and dependency ordering are documented. No files, branches, commits, or remotes were changed; no work is continuing.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/large_layer_human_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/large_layer_human_review/consolidate_1_50\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
