{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T11:52:48.668Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"GitHub’s stack API caps a stack at 100 pull requests. I’m therefore folding acceptance evidence into the feature it proves—rather than creating detached “catch-up test” PRs—and using the freed slots for the genuinely necessary code splits. That also fixes an intermediate-head compliance problem the deeper audit exposed. ([GitHub Stacked PR REST reference](https://github.github.com/gh-stack/reference/rest-api/))","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
