{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T11:54:12.235Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019fd6ec-838a-7681-a45d-c5ab76e9cd28","author":"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/branch_gate_audit_55_81\nPayload:\nRead-only audit complete; no checkout, edits, commits, remote operations, locks, or tests were performed.\n\nVerdict: positions 82, 84, 85, 87, 89, 90, and 93 require splits. Position 91 should also be hunk-split and routed back to its owning journey branches. It is only a defensible cohesive exception if cross-commit hunk routing is prohibited.\n\n## Position 82 — `993235de…`\n\nMandatory six-way split:\n\n1. `codex/82-member-role-administration`  \n   `test: prove member role administration` — 177 lines\n\n   - `tests/docs/roles/about-permissions.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/docs/roles/roles.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/admin/roles-management.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/admin/user-role-assignment.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/user-role-assignment-scenario.ts`\n\n2. `codex/82-member-onboarding`  \n   `test: prove member onboarding` — 126\n\n   - `tests/docs/users/tenant-onboarding.doc.ts`\n\n3. `codex/82-organization-settings`  \n   `test: prove organization settings` — 396\n\n   - `tests/specs/admin/general-settings.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/admin/google-maps-location.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/permissions/matrix.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/permissions/matrix.ts`\n\n4. `codex/82-semantic-theme-contrast`  \n   `test: prove semantic theme contrast` — 114\n\n   - `tests/specs/smoke/semantic-theme-colors.test.ts`\n\n5. `codex/82-platform-tenant-administration`  \n   `test: prove platform tenant administration` — 191\n\n   - `tests/specs/admin/global-admin-tenants.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/admin/platform-tenant-operations.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/permissions/global-admin-route-guard.spec.ts`\n\n6. `codex/82-email-delivery-administration`  \n   `test: prove email delivery administration` — 193\n\n   - `tests/specs/admin/email-outbox.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/email-outbox-scenario.ts`\n\nNo position-82 within-file split is needed. The email child must incorporate or immediately precede the position-83 email documentation update: the new helper drops `queued`, `retry`, and `exhausted` while the old doc still consumes them.\n\n## Position 84 — `909475f4…`\n\nMandatory split, with one small prerequisite hunk relocation:\n\n1. `codex/84-profile-pages`  \n   `test: prove profile pages` — 342, plus a two-line import replacement\n\n   Whole files:\n\n   - `tests/docs/profile/user-profile.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-edit.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-events.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-receipts.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/profile-event-cards.ts`\n\n   Also stage only the import-path replacement in `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts`:\n\n   - `profile/user-profile/user-profile.esn-card`\n   - → `profile/profile-discounts/profile-discounts.esn-card`\n\n   This repairs the deleted module path while the profile fixture changes repair the new receipt shape.\n\n2. `codex/84-esncard-discount-journeys`  \n   `test: prove ESNcard discount journeys` — remaining 641\n\n   - Remaining hunks of `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/discounts/esn-discounts.test.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-discounts.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-live-esncard.spec.ts`\n\n3. `codex/84-member-account-onboarding`  \n   `test: prove member account onboarding` — 71\n\n   - `tests/specs/profile/create-account.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/profile/tenant-onboarding.spec.ts`\n\nDo not create a ten-line position-84 child for `tests/support/utils/receipt-submission.ts`; fold that whole file into position 89’s receipt child, alongside both consumers.\n\n## Position 85 — `c22940a…`\n\nMandatory four-way split:\n\n1. `codex/85-event-discovery-eligibility`  \n   `test: prove event discovery eligibility` — 371\n\n   - `tests/specs/events/event-discovery-eligibility.test.ts`\n   - Only the filter-removal hunks from `tests/specs/events/events.test.ts`:\n     - remove `permissionOverride`\n     - remove the `Filter events` button assertions\n     - remove filter-dialog keyboard interaction\n\n2. `codex/85-manual-approval-journeys`  \n   `test: prove manual approval journeys` — 366\n\n   - `tests/docs/events/manual-approval.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/manual-approval.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/manual-approval-scenario.ts`\n\n3. `codex/85-organizer-helper-sign-up`  \n   `test: prove organizer and helper sign-up` — 225\n\n   - `tests/docs/events/organizer-signup.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/organizer-signup.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/organizer-signup-scenario.ts`\n\n4. `codex/85-template-category-journeys`  \n   `test: prove template and category journeys` — 438\n\n   - Remaining authoring/accessibility hunks of `tests/specs/events/events.test.ts`\n   - `tests/docs/template-categories/categories.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/docs/templates/templates.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/template-categories/template-categories.test.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/templates/paid-option-requires-tax-rate.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/templates/registration-configuration.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/templates/template-actions-permissions.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/templates/templates.test.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/template-form.ts`\n\nThe `events.test.ts` split is mandatory: discovery owns the removed filter workflow; template authoring owns sign-up-choice labels, selected-role labels, the role placeholder, and back-link assertions.\n\n## Position 87 — `4da5cd8f…`\n\nMandatory three-way split:\n\n1. `codex/87-registration-and-add-ons`  \n   `test: prove registration and add-on journeys` — 361\n\n   - `tests/docs/events/register.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/free-registration.test.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/negative-registration-states.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/price-labels-inclusive.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/registration-addons.test.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/event-registration-page.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/post-registration-addon-purchase-scenario.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/seed-registration-addons.ts`\n\n2. `codex/87-ticket-cancellation`  \n   `test: prove ticket cancellation lifecycle` — 504\n\n   - `tests/docs/events/registration-cancellation.doc.ts`\n\n3. `codex/87-ticket-transfer`  \n   `test: prove ticket transfer lifecycle` — 422\n\n   - `tests/docs/events/registration-transfer.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/events/registration-transfer.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/paid-registration-transfer-scenario.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/registration-transfer-claim-page.ts`\n\nAll are whole-file groups. The new claim-page utility must remain with both transfer consumers.\n\n## Position 89 — `d202d38b…`\n\nMandatory three-way split:\n\n1. `codex/89-finance-tax-rate-journeys`  \n   `test: prove finance and tax-rate journeys` — 298\n\n   - `tests/docs/finance/finance-overview.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/docs/finance/inclusive-tax-rates.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/finance/finance-overview-permissions.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/finance/tax-rates/admin-import-tax-rates.spec.ts`\n\n2. `codex/89-receipt-reimbursement-journeys`  \n   `test: prove receipt submission and reimbursement` — 354, or 364 after folding the position-84 helper\n\n   - `tests/docs/finance/receipt-review-reimbursement.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/docs/finance/receipt-submission.doc.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/finance/receipts-flows.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/receipt-submission.ts` from position 84\n\n3. `codex/89-stripe-webhook-recovery`  \n   `test: prove Stripe webhook recovery` — 291\n\n   - `tests/specs/finance/stripe-webhook-replay.spec.ts`\n\nNo hunk splits are needed.\n\n## Position 90 — `b75a13fb…`\n\nMandatory three-way whole-file split:\n\n1. `codex/90-generated-guide-language-contract`  \n   `test: enforce generated guide language` — 144\n\n   - `helpers/testing/generated-docs-language.spec.ts`\n   - `helpers/testing/generated-docs-language.ts`\n\n2. `codex/90-documentation-reporter-output`  \n   `test: harden generated documentation output` — 432\n\n   - `tests/specs/reporting/reporter-paths.test.ts`\n   - `tests/support/reporters/documentation-reporter.ts`\n   - `tests/support/reporters/documentation-reporter/attachments.ts`\n   - `tests/support/reporters/documentation-reporter/shared.ts`\n   - `tests/support/reporters/documentation-reporter/take-screenshot.ts`\n   - `tests/support/utils/doc-screenshot.ts`\n\n3. `codex/90-documentation-publication`  \n   `test: publish generated guides to the marketing site` — 559\n\n   - `helpers/testing/documentation-publication-contract.ts`\n   - `helpers/testing/publish-documentation.spec.ts`\n   - `helpers/testing/publish-documentation.ts`\n   - `tests/docs/users/create-account.doc.ts`\n\nOrder is strict: language contract → reporter → publication. Reporter attachments import the language helper; publication imports both the language contract and `buildDocumentationPage`.\n\n## Position 91 — `c3185ebd…`\n\nPreferred result:\n\n`codex/91-generated-guide-source-contract`  \n`test: guard generated guide sources` — 399 changed lines\n\nStage only final-file lines 1–410 of `helpers/testing/generated-docs-source.spec.ts`: imports, AST/source helpers, and the first seven generic tests covering language, captions, seed copy, organization identities, internal addresses, metadata/permissions, and ellipses.\n\nRoute every remaining hunk to its owning journey child:\n\n| Final test block | Changed lines | Destination |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Cancellation seed/waitlist/add-on cancellation, lines 432–851 | 67 | position 87 registration/cancellation children |\n| Organization settings, 852–931 | 92 | `codex/82-organization-settings` |\n| Unknown-domain recovery, 932–952 | 2 | position-83 discovery/admin docs child |\n| Global admin + platform operator, 953–1082 | 43 | `codex/82-platform-tenant-administration` |\n| Email outbox, 1083–1132 | 37 | `codex/82-email-delivery-administration` plus position 83 doc |\n| Profile docs, 1133–1217 | 38 | `codex/84-profile-pages` |\n| Account creation, 1218–1242 | 16 | `codex/90-documentation-publication` |\n| Tenant onboarding, 1243–1268 | 12 | `codex/82-member-onboarding` |\n| `tenant-onboarding-docs-source.spec.ts` | 6 | `codex/82-member-onboarding` |\n| Finance receipts, 1315–1346 | 14 | `codex/89-receipt-reimbursement-journeys` |\n| Finance overview/tax, 1347–1445 | 38 | `codex/89-finance-tax-rate-journeys` |\n| Templates/categories, 1446–1562 | 58 | `codex/85-template-category-journeys` |\n| Registration test, 1563–2056 | 172 | Split below |\n| Discovery, 2057–2095 | 68 | final position-85/86 discovery child |\n| Manual approval, 2096–2160 | 39 | `codex/85-manual-approval-journeys` |\n| Organizer sign-up, 2161–2225 | 29 | `codex/85-organizer-helper-sign-up` |\n| Event approval, 2226–2267 | 14 | position-86 publishing child |\n| Event management, 2268–2387 | 54 | split by its scanner/template/ticket assertions |\n| Check-in, 2388–2418 | 20 | position-88 scanning child |\n| Roles, 2419–2490 | 17 | `codex/82-member-role-administration` |\n| ESN discounts, 2491–end | 19 | `codex/84-esncard-discount-journeys` |\n\nWithin the 172-line registration block:\n\n- Final lines 1563–1690 and 1994–2056: 70 changed lines → registration/add-ons.\n- Final lines 1691–1993: 102 changed lines → ticket transfer.\n\nThis routing keeps the adjusted position-87 children around 439, 563, and 524 lines respectively.\n\nIf this hunk routing is disallowed, position 91 is the sole defensible cohesive exception: 1,254 changed lines across one monolithic source-contract spec and a six-line companion update. That exception is inferior because earlier journey branches retain knowingly stale assertions.\n\n## Position 93 — `2bca7342…`\n\nMandatory five-way split:\n\n1. `codex/93-administration-source-contracts`  \n   `test: align administration source contracts` — 57\n\n   - `helpers/testing/platform-authority-source.spec.ts`\n   - `helpers/testing/user-list-source.spec.ts`\n\n2. `codex/93-explicit-load-recovery`  \n   `test: prove explicit load recovery` — 61\n\n   - `tests/specs/resilience/core-load-recovery.spec.ts`\n   - `tests/specs/smoke/load-application.test.ts`\n\n3. `codex/93-plain-product-language`  \n   `test: enforce plain product language` — 427\n\n   - `src/app/plain-product-language.spec.ts`\n   - `helpers/testing/generated-docs-language.ts`\n\n4. `codex/93-playwright-acceptance-contract`  \n   `test: enforce the Playwright acceptance contract` — 419\n\n   - `helpers/testing/playwright-skip-inventory.spec.ts`\n   - `helpers/testing/provider-release-scope.spec.ts`\n   - `playwright.config.ts`\n   - `tests/README.md`\n   - `tests/test-inventory.md`\n\n5. `codex/93-lint-node-and-playwright-sources`  \n   `test: lint Node and Playwright sources` — 25\n\n   - `eslint.config.mjs`\n   - `helpers/testing/ci-quality-source.spec.ts`\n\nThese depend on position 92’s application-copy changes. Keep the inventory child after all test additions because its exact contract is 29 docs files and 45 spec files. Keep the lint child last so extending lint to `tests/**/*.ts` evaluates the final test tree.\n\nOverall, the recommended history needs no >700-line exception. The only unavoidable-looking oversized commit, position 91, becomes a 399-line generic source-contract child plus small expectation hunks co-located with the behaviors they protect.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
