cal-database-operations-fail-closed`, `fix: make local database operations fail closed`; 31 files, +924/-235, total 1,159; reduction 2 instead of 1.\\n- Old 30–32: `codex/add-private-organization-payment-setup`, `feat: add and prove private organization payment setup`; 10 files, +1,522/-12, total 1,534; reduction 2. Strong implementation + PostgreSQL serialization proof + private route, but a documented size exception.\\n- Old 44–45: `codex/harden-auth-and-onboarding-identity`, `fix: harden auth and onboarding identity boundaries`; 19 files, +934/-310, total 1,244; reduction 1. Old 44 is already +802, so the +132 onboarding follow-up is a reasonable atomic addition.\\n- Old 48–49: `codex/make-scaleway-releases-fail-closed-and-forward-only`, `fix: make Scaleway releases fail closed and forward only`; 12 files, +866/-348, total 1,214; reduction 1. Slightly above target but highly cohesive release-safety work.\\n- Eliminate old 50 by distributing its two corrective files: put `helpers/testing/stripe-webhook-secret.ts` into old 21’s distroless-runtime layer and `.env.dev.local` into old 44’s 32-byte auth-secret layer. This removes 1 layer while making both fixes local to their causes.\\n- Extending the migration deletion unit through old 13 yields 59 files, +15/-9,891, total 9,906 and one additional reduction, but the invalid `@types/*` alias is less cohesive than the migration removals.\\n\\n## Important non-fold\\n\\nKeep old 46 and 47 separate. Position 46 explicitly prepares isolated Terraform roots “without changing current releases”; position 47 performs the workflow/backend cutover. That is a deliberate operational prepare/cutover boundary, not review fragmentation.\\n\\nConservative result: 19 reductions from positions 1–50. Accepting every reserve can raise this contribution to 26, though the 19-layer set is the cleaner human-review baseline.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
