ts both the language contract and `buildDocumentationPage`.\\n\\n## Position 91 — `c3185ebd…`\\n\\nPreferred result:\\n\\n`codex/91-generated-guide-source-contract`  \\n`test: guard generated guide sources` — 399 changed lines\\n\\nStage only final-file lines 1–410 of `helpers/testing/generated-docs-source.spec.ts`: imports, AST/source helpers, and the first seven generic tests covering language, captions, seed copy, organization identities, internal addresses, metadata/permissions, and ellipses.\\n\\nRoute every remaining hunk to its owning journey child:\\n\\n| Final test block | Changed lines | Destination |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Cancellation seed/waitlist/add-on cancellation, lines 432–851 | 67 | position 87 registration/cancellation children |\\n| Organization settings, 852–931 | 92 | `codex/82-organization-settings` |\\n| Unknown-domain recovery, 932–952 | 2 | position-83 discovery/admin docs child |\\n| Global admin + platform operator, 953–1082 | 43 | `codex/82-platform-tenant-administration` |\\n| Email outbox, 1083–1132 | 37 | `codex/82-email-delivery-administration` plus position 83 doc |\\n| Profile docs, 1133–1217 | 38 | `codex/84-profile-pages` |\\n| Account creation, 1218–1242 | 16 | `codex/90-documentation-publication` |\\n| Tenant onboarding, 1243–1268 | 12 | `codex/82-member-onboarding` |\\n| `tenant-onboarding-docs-source.spec.ts` | 6 | `codex/82-member-onboarding` |\\n| Finance receipts, 1315–1346 | 14 | `codex/89-receipt-reimbursement-journeys` |\\n| Finance overview/tax, 1347–1445 | 38 | `codex/89-finance-tax-rate-journeys` |\\n| Templates/categories, 1446–1562 | 58 | `codex/85-template-category-journeys` |\\n| Registration test, 1563–2056 | 172 | Split below |\\n| Discovery, 2057–2095 | 68 | final position-85/86 discovery child |\\n| Manual approval, 2096–2160 | 39 | `codex/85-manual-approval-journeys` |\\n| Organizer sign-up, 2161–2225 | 29 | `codex/85-organizer-helper-sign-up` |\\n| Event approval, 2226–2267 | 14 | position-86 publishing child |\\n| Event management, 2268–2387 | 54 | split by its scanner/template/ticket assertions |\\n| Check-in, 2388–2418 | 20 | position-88 scanning child |\\n| Roles, 2419–2490 | 17 | `codex/82-member-role-administration` |\\n| ESN discounts, 2491–end | 19 | `codex/84-esncard-discount-journeys` |\\n\\nWithin the 172-line registration block:\\n\\n- Final lines 1563–1690 and 1994–2056: 70 changed lines → registration/add-ons.\\n- Final lines 1691–1993: 102 changed lines → ticket transfer.\\n\\nThis routing keeps the adjusted position-87 children around 439, 563, and 524 lines respectively.\\n\\nIf this hunk routing is disallowed, position 91 is the sole defensible cohesive exception: 1,254 changed lines across one monolithic source-contract spec and a six-line companion update. That exception is inferior because earlier journey branches retain knowingly stale assertions.\\n\\n## Position 93 — `2bca7342…`\\n\\nMandatory five-way split:\\n\\n1. `codex/93-administration-source-contracts`  \\n   `test: align administration source contracts` — 57\\n\\n   - `helpers/testing/platform-authority-source.spec.ts`\\n   - `helpers/testing/user-list-source.spec.ts`\\n\\n2. `codex/93-explicit-load-recovery`  \\n   `test: prove explicit load recovery` — 61\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/resilience/core-load-recovery.spec.ts`\\n   - `tests/specs/smoke/load-application.test.ts`\\n\\n3. `codex/93-plain-product-language`  \\n   `test: enforce plain product language` — 427\\n\\n   - `src/app/plain-product-language.spec.ts`\\n   - `helpers/testing/generated-docs-language.ts`\\n\\n4. `codex/93-playwright-acceptance-contract`  \\n   `test: enforce the Playwright acceptance contract` — 419\\n\\n   - `helpers/testing/playwright-skip-inventory.spec.ts`\\n   - `helpers/testing/provider-release-scope.spec.ts`\\n   - `playwright.config.ts`\\n   - `tests/README.md`\\n   - `tests/test-inventory.md`\\n\\n5. `codex/93-lint-node-and-playwright-sources`  \\n   `test: lint Node and Playwright sources` — 25\\n\\n   - `eslint.config.mjs`\\n   - `helpers/testing/ci-quality-source.spec.ts`\\n\\nThese depend on position 92’s application-copy changes. Keep the inventory child after all test additions because its exact contract is 29 docs files and 45 spec files. Keep the lint child last so extending lint to `tests/**/*.ts` evaluates the final test tree.\\n\\nOverall, the recommended history needs no >700-line exception. The only unavoidable-looking oversized commit, position 91, becomes a 399-line generic source-contract child plus small expectation hunks co-located with the behaviors they protect.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/branch_gate_audit_55_81/split_82_84\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Audited both exact first-parent diffs read-only. No tests were run.\\n\\n## `993235de…` — position 82\\n\\nParent: `9cc62767d925bc380f7ec89a06b3b3be99bd1eaf`  \\nTotal: `+692/-505 = 1,197` changed lines across 16 files.\\n\\nVerdict: mandatory split. It exceeds 700 lines and contains six independent journeys; no cohesive exception is defensible.\\n\\n1. `codex/82-member-role-administration`  \\n   `test: prove member role administration`  \\n   `+99/-78 = 177`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/roles/about-permissions.doc.ts` — 11\\n   - `tests/docs/roles/roles.doc.ts` — 135\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/roles-management.spec.ts` — 15\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/user-role-assignment.spec.ts` — 10\\n   - `tests/support/utils/user-role-assignment-scenario.ts` — 6\\n\\n2. `codex/82-member-onboarding`  \\n   `test: prove member onboarding`  \\n   `+56/-70 = 126`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/users/tenant-onboarding.doc.ts` — 126\\n\\n3. `codex/82-organization-settings`  \\n   `test: prove organization settings`  \\n   `+238/-158 = 396`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/general-settings.spec.ts` — 362\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/google-maps-location.spec.ts` — 8\\n   - `tests/specs/permissions/matrix.spec.ts` — 7\\n   - `tests/support/permissions/matrix.ts` — 19\\n\\n4. `codex/82-semantic-theme-contrast`  \\n   `test: prove semantic theme contrast`  \\n   `+106/-8 = 114`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/smoke/semantic-theme-colors.test.ts` — 114\\n\\n5. `codex/82-platform-tenant-administration`  \\n   `test: prove platform tenant administration`  \\n   `+114/-77 = 191`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/global-admin-tenants.spec.ts` — 132\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/platform-tenant-operations.spec.ts` — 35\\n   - `tests/specs/permissions/global-admin-route-guard.spec.ts` — 24\\n\\n6. `codex/82-email-delivery-administration`  \\n   `test: prove email delivery administration`  \\n   `+79/-114 = 193`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/admin/email-outbox.spec.ts` — 86\\n   - `tests/support/utils/email-outbox-scenario.ts` — 107\\n\\nDependencies/order:\\n\\n- Files are disjoint between children. Shared data and consumer tests remain together.\\n- Keep the email child last. At `993235de…`, `EmailOutboxScenario` exposes only `failed`, `unknown`, `sending`, and `sent` at helper lines 17–22, while unchanged `tests/docs/admin/email-outbox.doc.ts:77-80,145` still accesses `queued`, `retry`, and `exhausted`.\\n- The following commit, `cc125768…`, repairs that documentation consumer. Therefore child 6 and the original unsplit position-82 commit are not typecheck/full-suite plausible in isolation.\\n- Children 1–5 are statically plausible individually, but full Playwright plausibility is low because untouched catch-up tests still target UI changed by earlier application commits. Targeted suites are the credible intermediate checks.\\n- No within-file split is recommended. Keep the complete `global admin route guard allow/deny path` suites in child 5, including Email delivery and audit routes, because they form one platform route-guard inventory. Keep the single multi-step general-settings test intact in child 3.\\n\\n## `909475f4…` — position 84\\n\\nParent: `cc125768705c784f20ab22862635d6b47654411c`  \\nTotal: `+615/-451 = 1,066` changed lines across 12 files.\\n\\nVerdict: mandatory split. It combines ESNcard, general profile, onboarding, and organizer receipt-form journeys.\\n\\n1. `codex/84-esncard-discount-journeys`  \\n   `test: prove ESNcard discount journeys`  \\n   `+353/-290 = 643`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts` — 325\\n   - `tests/specs/discounts/esn-discounts.test.ts` — 2\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-discounts.spec.ts` — 52\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-live-esncard.spec.ts` — 264\\n\\n2. `codex/84-profile-pages`  \\n   `test: prove profile pages`  \\n   `+221/-121 = 342`\\n\\n   - `tests/docs/profile/user-profile.doc.ts` — 155\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-edit.spec.ts` — 16\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-events.spec.ts` — 21\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/user-profile-receipts.spec.ts` — 12\\n   - `tests/support/utils/profile-event-cards.ts` — 138\\n\\n3. `codex/84-member-account-onboarding`  \\n   `test: prove member account onboarding`  \\n   `+37/-34 = 71`\\n\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/create-account.spec.ts` — 19\\n   - `tests/specs/profile/tenant-onboarding.spec.ts` — 52\\n\\n4. `codex/84-receipt-submission-controls`  \\n   `test: align receipt submission controls`  \\n   `+4/-6 = 10`\\n\\n   - `tests/support/utils/receipt-submission.ts` — 10\\n\\nDependencies/order:\\n\\n- Child 1 should be first: its parent’s `tests/docs/profile/discounts.doc.ts:12` imports the deleted `profile/user-profile/user-profile.esn-card` path; the actual module is already under `profile/profile-discounts/`.\\n- Static checks likely remain red until child 2. The parent schema requires `alcoholAmount`, `depositAmount`, `hasAlcohol`, `hasDeposit`, and a date-string `receiptDate`; child 2 updates the stale receipt inserts and profile-event fixture snapshots.\\n- Children 3 and 4 are runtime-selector/content alignments and have no code dependency on each other.\\n- Full suite plausibility starts only after all four. Child 1’s live ESNcard coverage additionally requires the credential-gated provider suite; non-live ESNcard tests are the plausible intermediate evidence.\\n- Child 4 must exercise its unchanged consumers: `tests/docs/finance/receipt-submission.doc.ts` and `tests/specs/finance/receipts-flows.spec.ts`.\\n- No within-file split is recommended. Keep the entire `Manage your profile` documentation test in child 2 because its shared setup/cleanup deliberately traverses overview, events, and receipts. Keep all three ESNcard documentation blocks—status, managed card, and live-provider flow—in child 1; the 643-line child remains below the limit and is one cohesive domain journey.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/event_discovery_templates/final_source_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/large_layer_human_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only consolidation plan sent to the coordinator.\\n\\nIt yields exactly 100 layers:\\n\\n- 100 current layers\\n- +35 required split layers\\n- −5 absorbed late catch-up layers\\n- −30 focused early consolidations\\n- = 100 draft PRs\\n\\nAll proposed PRs remain under 100 files. I also flagged the email-outbox schema contraction and several stale test/documentation consumers that must be repaired within their owning implementation PR to keep every stack head green. No repository state was changed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/large_layer_human_review/consolidate_1_50\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Verified the local `gh stack view --json`: exactly 100 layers; positions 1–50 match the requested range. No checkout, edit, ref, fetch, or remote mutation occurred. Counts below use combined `git diff --numstat`; total = additions + deletions.\\n\\n## Conservative consolidation: 19 reductions\\n\\n1. Old 1–2\\n\\n   - `codex/remove-prior-compliance-artifacts`\\n   - `codex/remove-dead-runtime-dependencies`\\n   - Proposed: `codex/remove-retired-compliance-and-runtime-artifacts`\\n   - Title: `refactor: remove retired compliance and runtime artifacts`\\n   - 16 files, +20/-1,651, total 1,671\\n   - Reduction: 1\\n   - Adjacent. Both