ansfer-refund-recovery`\\n   - `codex/guard-transfer-acquisition-data`\\n   - Proposed: `codex/harden-transfer-refund-and-acquisition-integrity`\\n   - Title: `fix: harden transfer refund and acquisition integrity`\\n   - 13 files, +551/-151, total 702\\n   - Reduction: 1\\n   - Adjacent; keep after old 24’s transfer rules. The tiny acquisition guard completes the refund/transfer lifecycle integrity work.\\n\\n6. Old 27–29\\n\\n   - `codex/remove-direct-registration-reassignment`\\n   - `codex/use-private-registration-transfer-claims`\\n   - `codex/add-private-transfer-claim-interface`\\n   - Proposed: `codex/replace-direct-registration-reassignment`\\n   - Title: `feat: replace direct reassignment with private transfer claims`\\n   - 27 files, +716/-722, total 1,438\\n   - Reduction: 2\\n   - Adjacent vertical slice: remove unsafe RPC, implement private claim codes server-side, expose the claim UI. Keep after 24–26.\\n\\n7. Old 34 and 36\\n\\n   - `codex/report-client-failures-safely`\\n   - `codex/clarify-application-access-boundaries`\\n   - Proposed: `codex/make-client-failures-and-access-denial-explicit`\\n   - Title: `fix: make client failures and access denial explicit`\\n   - 35 files, +561/-171, total 732\\n   - Reduction: 1\\n   - Move old 36 before old 35. Old 35 is path-disjoint from 36, while 34 and 36 meet naturally in members-hub/error/access-denial behavior. Leave `codex/simplify-shared-form-controls` afterward.\\n\\n8. Old 38 and 40\\n\\n   - `codex/make-scanner-recovery-explicit`\\n   - `codex/harden-ticket-qr-responses`\\n   - Proposed: `codex/harden-scanner-recovery-and-qr-responses`\\n   - Title: `fix: make scanner recovery explicit and harden QR responses`\\n   - 14 files, +792/-336, total 1,128\\n   - Reduction: 1\\n   - Move old 40 before old 39. Positions 39 and 40 are path-disjoint; recovery and QR response hardening form the safety boundary, while old 39 remains a separate language refactor.\\n\\n9. Old 41–42\\n\\n   - `codex/validate-tenant-website-addresses`\\n   - `codex/explain-blocked-tenant-integrity-changes`\\n   - Proposed: `codex/validate-and-explain-tenant-integrity`\\n   - Title: `fix: validate and explain blocked tenant integrity changes`\\n   - 12 files, +273/-135, total 408\\n   - Reduction: 1\\n   - Adjacent. URL validation and explicit blocked public-URL/currency integrity outcomes belong in one review.\\n\\n## Optional atomic exceptions\\n\\nNot included in the conservative 19:\\n\\n- Replace 15–16 with old 14–16: `codex/make-local-database-operations-fail-closed`, `fix: make local database operations fail closed`; 31 files, +924/-235, total 1,159; reduction 2 instead of 1.\\n- Old 30–32: `codex/add-private-organization-payment-setup`, `feat: add and prove private organization payment setup`; 10 files, +1,522/-12, total 1,534; reduction 2. Strong implementation + PostgreSQL serialization proof + private route, but a documented size exception.\\n- Old 44–45: `codex/harden-auth-and-onboarding-identity`, `fix: harden auth and onboarding identity boundaries`; 19 files, +934/-310, total 1,244; reduction 1. Old 44 is already +802, so the +132 onboarding follow-up is a reasonable atomic addition.\\n- Old 48–49: `codex/make-scaleway-releases-fail-closed-and-forward-only`, `fix: make Scaleway releases fail closed and forward only`; 12 files, +866/-348, total 1,214; reduction 1. Slightly above target but highly cohesive release-safety work.\\n- Eliminate old 50 by distributing its two corrective files: put `helpers/testing/stripe-webhook-secret.ts` into old 21’s distroless-runtime layer and `.env.dev.local` into old 44’s 32-byte auth-secret layer. This removes 1 layer while making both fixes local to their causes.\\n- Extending the migration deletion unit through old 13 yields 59 files, +15/-9,891, total 9,906 and one additional reduction, but the invalid `@types/*` alias is less cohesive than the migration removals.\\n\\n## Important non-fold\\n\\nKeep old 46 and 47 separate. Position 46 explicitly prepares isolated Terraform roots “without changing current releases”; position 47 performs the workflow/backend cutover. That is a deliberate operational prepare/cutover boundary, not review fragmentation.\\n\\nConservative result: 19 reductions from positions 1–50. Accepting every reserve can raise this contribution to 26, though the 19-layer set is the cleaner human-review baseline.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
